154BA c  2017Wu04: The {+154}Ba nuclide was produced at the RIBF-RIKEN facility 
154BA2c  using the {+9}Be({+238}U,F) reaction at E=345 MeV/nucleon.  Two        
154BA3c  experiments, optimized for the transmission of {+158}Nd and {+170}Dy   
154BA4c  ions, were carried out with average beam intensities of 7 pnA and 12   
154BA5c  pnA, respectively. The identification of the nuclide of interest was   
154BA6c  made in the BigRIPS separator by determining the atomic number and the 
154BA7c  mass-to-charge ratio of the ion using the tof-B|r-|DE method. The      
154BA8c  reaction products were transported through the ZeroDegree Spectrometer 
154BA9c  and implanted into the beta-counting system WAS3ABi that was surrounded
154BAac  by the EURICA array comprising of 84 HPGe detectors. The typical       
154BAbc  implantation rate was ~~100 ions/s.  Measured: implanted ion-|b{+-}-t, 
154BAcc  implanted ion-|b{+-}-|g-t and implanted ions-|g-t correlations.        
154BAdc  Deduced: T{-1/2}.                                                      
154BA c  2018Fu08, 2018Sh11: like 2017Wu04, with only two {+154}Ba events       
154BA2c  selected                                                               
154BA  L 0.0          0+               53 MS     48                             
154BA2 L %B-=100 $ %B-N=?                                                       
154BA cL %B-$Only |b{+-} decay mode is expected.                                
154BA cL T$From 2017Wu04, using a fit to the implanted ion-|b{+-}-t spectrum    
154BA2cL using the least-squares and maximum-likelihood methods. The data       
154BA3cL analysis included contributions from the parent, daughter and          
154BA4cL ground-daughter decays, as well as a constant background.              

