154LA c  2017Wu04: The {+154}La nuclide was produced at the RIBF-RIKEN facility 
154LA2c  using the {+9}Be({+238}U,F) reaction at E=345 MeV/nucleon.  Two        
154LA3c  experiments, optimized for the transmission of {+158}Nd and {+170}Dy   
154LA4c  ions, were carried out with average beam intensities of 7 pnA and 12   
154LA5c  pnA, respectively. The identification of the nuclide of interest was   
154LA6c  made in the BigRIPS separator by determining the atomic number and the 
154LA7c  mass-to-charge ratio of the ion using the tof-B|r-|DE method. The      
154LA8c  reaction products were transported through the ZeroDegree Spectrometer 
154LA9c  and implanted into the beta-counting system WAS3ABi that was surrounded
154LAac  by the EURICA array comprising of 84 HPGe detectors. The typical       
154LAbc  implantation rate was ~~100 ions/s.  Measured: implanted ion-|b{+-}-t, 
154LAcc  implanted ion-|b{+-}-|g-t and implanted ions-|g-t correlations.        
154LAdc  Deduced: T{-1/2}.                                                      
154LA c  2020Wu04: {+154}La nuclide produced at the RIBF-RIKEN facility by      
154LA2c  {+9}Be({+238}U,F) reaction at E=345 MeV/nucleon and an intensity of    
154LA3c  5 pnA. Identification of fission fragments of interest was made based  
154LA4c  on time-of-flight (tof), magnetic rigidity (B|r), and energy loss (|DE)
154LA5c  using the BigRIPS spectrometer, determining atomic Z and mass-to-charge
154LA6c  ratio A/Q, where Q=charge state of the ions. The separated nuclei      
154LA7c  were implanted at a rate of 100 ions/s in the beta counting system     
154LA8c  of the Wide range Active Silicon-Strip Stopper Array for Beta and      
154LA9c  ion detection (WAS3ABi), which included a stack of five Double Sided   
154LAAc  Silicon Strip Detectors (DSSSDs). The WAS3ABi setup was surrounded     
154LABc  by Euroball Riken Cluster Array (EURICA) array of 84 HPGe detectors    
154LACc  for |g detection. Half-life of the separated and implanted ions        
154LADc  was determined by fitting the time distribution of |b(implants)- and/or
154LAEc  |b|g(implants)-correlated decay curves to the sum of activities of     
154LAFc  parent nuclei, daughter nuclei, grand-daughter nuclei, |b-delayed      
154LAGc  neutron daughter and grand-daughter nuclei, and a constant background. 
154LAHc  Comparison of measured half-lives with FRDM+QRPA (2003), FRDM+QRPA     
154LAIc  (2019), KTUY+GT2, RHB+pn-RQRPA, and DF+CQRPA theoretical calculations. 
154LA c  Others: 2018Fu08, 2018Sh11                                             
154LA  L 0.0          (2-)             161 MS    15                             
154LA2 L %B-=100 $ %B-N=?                                                       
154LA cL %B-$Only |b{+-} decay mode is expected.                                
154LA cL J$From systematics of known quasiparticle states in neighboring nuclei 
154LA2cL and the proposed configuration (by the evaluator). The assignment is   
154LA3cL tentative.                                                             
154LA cL T$from 2017Wu04, by using a fit to the implanted                       
154LA2cL ion-|b{+-}-t spectrum                                                  
154LA2cL using the least-squares and maximum-likelihood methods. The data       
154LA3cL analysis included contributions from the parent, daughter and          
154LA4cL grand-daughter decays, as well as a constant background.               
154LA4cL Other result: 221 ms {I89} (2020Wu04),                                 
154LA2cL assumed to correspond to {+154}La g.s., by fitting the                 
154LA2cL time distribution of                                                   
154LA2cL (implanted ions)|b-correlated decay curves to the sum of activities    
154LA3cL of parent nuclei, daughter nuclei, grand-daughter nuclei, |b{+-}n      
154LA4cL daughter and grand-daughter nuclei, and a constant background.         
154LA2cL The production of {+154}La of 2017Wu04 is about 100 stronger compared  
154LA2cL to 2020Wu04 leading to the more precise measurement that was adopted   
154LA cL CONF$From systematics of well-deformed nuclei in this mass region, the 
154LA2cL |p1/2[420] and |n5/2[523] Nilsson orbitals are expected near the proton
154LA3cL and neutron Fermi surfaces, respectively. Thus, using the              
154LA4cL Gallagher-Moszkowski rule, one may expect the K|p=2-,                  
154LA5cL |p1/2[420]~#|n5/2[523] configuration for the ground state.             
154LA7cL The assignment is tentative and it is made by the evaluator.           
154LA cL $2018Fu08: 2080 {+154}La counts; 2018Sh11 141 {+154}La counts          

