154PR2cL |p3/2[541]~#|n3/2[521]                                                 
154PR dL J$1996To05 suggest log| {Ift} values of|?5.8 and|?6.4 for the |b{+-}   
154PR2dL transitions to the first 2+ and 4+ levels, respectively, in {+154}Nd.  
154PR3dL This would indicate J{+|p}=3+ for the {+154}Pr g.s. however, a more    
154PR4dL complete decay scheme, with more reliable intensity balances, is needed
154PR5dL before a firm conclusion can be drawn. REJECYED BY F KONDEV:           
154PR5dL This is DK=3 forbiddenn transition and I'd expect log ft ~8-10         
154PR cL T$weighted average of 2.3 s {I1} (from I|g(t) and Ix(t) (1988Ka16,     
154PR2cL 1990Ok04, 1996To05)) and 2.29 s {I20} (2017Wu04)                       
154PR cL %B-$assumed to be 100%, since other decay modes seem to be unlikely    
154PR cL CONF$From systematics of well-deformed nuclei in this mass region, the 
154PR2cL |p3/2[541] and |n3/2[521] Nilsson orbitals are expected near the proton
154PR3cL and neutron Fermi surfaces, respectively. Thus, using the              
154PR4cL Gallagher-Moszkowski rule, one may expect the K|p=3+,                  
154PR5cL |p3/2[541]~#|n3/2[521] configuration for the ground state. The         
154PR6cL existence of a K|p=0+ isomer, arising from the same configuration, is  
154PR7cL also possible.                                                         

