154ND c  The level scheme is that proposed by 1998Zh12. It is in essential      
154ND2c       agreement with, but considerably more extensive than, the         
154ND3c       studies of 1995Zh39 and 1994Sm07, who report only the gs (yrast)  
154ND4c       band up through the 16+ level. 1998Ga12 add another level.        
154ND c            All studies involve the spontaneous fission of {+252}Cf,     
154ND2c       except that of 1994Sm07 which is from the spontaneous fission     
154ND3c       of {+148}Cm.                                                      
154ND c  1998Zh12: experimental details are not given, but are presumably       
154ND2c       similar to those of 1995Zh39.                                     
154ND c  1998Ga12: |g's measured in Eurogam II array with 54 Compton-suppressed 
154ND2c       Ge detectors. Authors report two delayed |g's (T{-1/2} > 1 |ms).  
154ND c  1995Zh39: |g|g and |g|g|g coincidences were measured using an array    
154ND2c       of 20 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors in an early version of      
154ND6c       Gammasphere having 36 Ge detectors and one LEPS detector.         
154ND c  1994Sm07: study the |g rays produced in the spontaneous fission        
154ND2c       of {+248}Cm. The Eurogam phase 1 array of Compton-suppressed      
154ND3c       Ge detectors was used. Measured level lifetimes by a modified     
154ND4c       DSAM technique (the Doppler profile method).                      
154ND c  1974JaYY:  Measured |g(t). See also 1974JaZN, by the same authors.     
154ND c  1973TaZG:  Measured E|g and |g(t).                                     
154ND c  1972Ho08:  Measured E|g.                                               
154ND c  1972ClZN:  Measured E|g. See also 1974ClZX, by the same authors.       
154ND c  1971Ch44: measured E|g and |g(t). Also 1970ChYJ, 1970ChZH, 1970ChZM,   
154ND2c       and 1970Wi16 from the same authors.                               
154ND c  1970Jo20:  Measured E|g and |g(t), but Z not unique.                   
