154ND  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154ND c  Includes studies of delayed |g rays from {+239}Pu(n,F|g) and from      
154ND2c  {+238}U SF decay as well as of prompt |g rays from {+252}Cf SF decay   
154ND c  2009Si21 was compiled for XUNDL database by B. Karamy and B. Singh     
154ND2c  (McMaster)                                                             
154ND c  2009Si21: delayed |g rays from {+154}Nd produced by {+239}Pu(n,F|g)    
154ND2c  reaction were detected by two clover Ge detectors                      
154ND2c  using the Lohengrin mass spectrometer of high-flux reactor of ILL,     
154ND3c  Grenoble. The mass spectrometer was used to select nuclei recoiling    
154ND4c  according to their mass-to-ion-charge and kinetic energy of the ion    
154ND5c  ratios. The time of flight through the spectrometer was |?2.7 |ms.     
154ND6c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, and half-lives.                               
154ND7c  Comparison with QRPM calculations.                                     
154ND c  2009Si21: {+252}Cf SF decay study, measured E|g, I|g, |g|g using       
154ND2c  Gammasphere array at ANL. Prompt |g rays measured.                     
154ND c  2012YoZZ, 2013YoZZ: in-flight fission of 345 MeV/nucleon {+238}U beam. 
154ND2c  Radioactive ion beams identified in so called PID plot by proton number
154ND2c  (Z) versus mass-to-charge ratio (A/Q) obtained by measurement          
154ND2c  of the magnetic rigidity (B|r), time of flight (tof), and              
154ND2c  energy loss (dE) in the BigRIPS separator. Used total kinetic          
154ND2c  energy (TKE) detector (20 layers of Si detectors) in the F12 focal     
154ND2c  plane at the end of the BigRIPS beamline, in order to identify heavier 
154ND2c  elements with different atomic charge states. Measured delayed |g rays 
154ND2c  135.5, 162.1, 270.0, 294.6, 794.0, 894.7, 931.0, 957.2 (with no        
154ND2c  uncertainty) and deduced T{-1/2}.                                      
154ND c  No evidence was found by 2009Si21 for a (5-) isomer with T{-1/2}>1 |ms 
154ND2c  reported in 1998Ga12.                                                  
154ND cG E$Delayed |g-ray energies are from {+239}Pu(n,F|g) and prompt |g-ray   
154ND2cG energies are from {+252}Cf SF decay (2009Si21).                        
