154PM  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154PM dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 28-Aug-2024)          
154PM c  The decay scheme, E|g, I|g are from 1993GrZZ and the measured |b{+-}   
154PM2c    data are from 1995Gr19 and 1997Gr09 (all by the same authors),       
154PM3c    unless otherwise noted. Other: 1985Ka17. Activity also               
154PM4c    identified by 1974Bu09. Earlier articles by the same authors as      
154PM5c    1993GrZZ are 1990An31, 1988GrZY, 1987Gr12, 1986GrZW, and 1986GrZZ.   
154PM D  Experimental methods:                                                  
154PM c  1974Bu09: Produced by {+235}U(th n,F), followed by chemical separation.
154PM2c    Established parentage.                                               
154PM c  1985Ka17: Produced by {+235}U(th n,F), followed by isotope separation. 
154PM2c    Parentage of {+154}Pm (1.7 min) established; and 19 |g's reported.   
154PM c  1986GrZW, 1993GrZZ: Produced by spontaneous fission of {+252}Cf,       
154PM2c    followed by isotope separation. |g's measured with Ge detectors.     
154PM3c    50 |g's reported. (Both references are private communications.)      
154PM c  1987Gr12: Produced by spontaneous fission of {+252}Cf, followed by     
154PM2c    isotope separation. Parent half-life and 13 |g energies reported.    
154PM c  1990An31: Produced by spontaneous fission of {+252}Cf, followed by     
154PM2c    isotope separation. Level scheme is shown.                           
154PM c  1995Gr19, 1997Gr09: Produced by spontaneous fission of {+252}Cf,       
154PM2c    followed by isotope separation. Deduced I|b{+-} to excited states    
154PM3c    and ground state from total absorption |g spectra.                   
154PM cB $This decay scheme is given here with its lowest (1-) level shown as   
154PM2cB being at 0+x keV. This level is more likely an isomer, as              
154PM3cB discussed in the {+154}Pm Adopted Levels, with the                     
154PM3cB (4+) state as g.s. Consequently the E(decay) values are smaller by the 
154PM3cB "x" value (based on the estimates in Adopted Levels this is of the     
154PM3cB order of 30 keV {I10}), which also can slightly affect the log| {Ift}  
154PM3cB calculations (more importantly for the higher excited levels)          
154PM3cB From this reason the calculated |b-decay parameters shown in the       
154PM3cB table should be used rather prudently.                                 
154PM cB           The I|b{+-} to the excited levels have been deduced,         
154PM2cB      independently of the |g data, from the total absorption |g        
154PM3cB      spectrometer, TAGS, data of 1997Gr09. When necessary, new         
154PM4cB      levels, called "pseudolevels", and associated decay |g's are      
154PM5cB      included in the analysis. Since the resolution of the TAGS        
154PM6cB      system is typically 50-100 keV, the intensity assigned to a       
154PM7cB      pseudolevel may thus represent the |b{+-} feeding to a single     
154PM8cB      level or to a group of levels in that region.                     
154PM cB IB        Values are from |g intensity balances, except those          
154PM2cB      for the 0- and 79-keV levels, which are from measurements of      
154PM3cB      1995Gr19. The I|b{+-} values from the TAGS data (1997Gr09) are    
154PM4cB      generally in excellent agreement with those from the intensity    
154PM5cB      balances. The TAGS value is given in a comment if it differs      
154PM6cB      by more than 10%.  Since the scheme is not complete, values       
154PM7cB      less than 0.2% are not given. Values for                          
154PM8cB      levels at 50, 68, and 105 keV are assumed to be 0.                
154PM cB IB        The pseudolevels and the associated I|b{+-} from the TAGS    
154PM2cB      data analysis are 1270 keV, 0.4%; 1470, 0.6; 1550, 0.8%; 1800,    
154PM3cB      0.3%; and 1900, 0.3%.                                             
154PM cG E         From 1993GrZZ.                                               
154PM cG RI        From 1993GrZZ. Values have not been corrected for            
154PM2cG      coincidence summing, which in the worst cases could be as         
154PM3cG      large as 30%.                                                     
154PM cG M$Same values as the {+154}Pm Adopted Gammas, based on data of         
154PM2cG 1993GrZZ, from |a{-K}(exp), from IKx/I|g ratio or from                 
154PM3cG |a(exp) based on intensity balances from |g|g coincidence              
154PM4cG spectra.                                                               
154PM cG E(R)      Existence and placement of |g is questionable.               
154PM cL E         From least-squares fit to |g energies, with questionable     
154PM2cL      |g's omitted.                                                     
