154SM c  The data on E|g and I|g values and J{+|p} assignments are primarily    
154SM2c  from the {+154}Pm |b{+-} decays (1.73~min and 2.68~min)                
154SM3c  (1971Da28,1974Ya07,1993GrZY) and the (n,n'|g) reaction (2006De19).     
154SM cG           The unplaced |g's are not given here, see {+154}Pm |g-       
154SM2cG      decay (1.73 m and 2.68 m) and {+154}Sm(n,n'|g).                   
154SM cG $Above 2430 the B(E1)(W.u.) and B(M1)(W.u.) values are deduced         
154SM2cG by the evaluator from the B(E1)|^ and B(M1)|^ values in the            
154SM2cG {+154}Sm(|g,|g'),(e,e') dataset                                        
154SM cG E         Values are from the measurement giving the most precise      
154SM2cG      value. This is often the {+154}Sm(n,n'|g) reaction or one of      
154SM3cG      the {+154}Pm |b{+-} decays.                                       
154SM cG RI$Unless mentioned otherwise, from {+154}Pm |b{+-} decays (1971Da28,  
154SM2cG 1974Ya07, 1993GrZY) and (n,n'|g) (1986Be52).                           
154SM cG M         From ce data following Coulomb excitation (1970Da28) and     
154SM2cG    (n,n'|g), unless noted otherwise.                                   
154SM cG CC(a)$|a(E0+M1+E2) = |a(E0)+|a(M1)+|a(E2) with                         
154SM2cG |a(E0) = |a{-K}(E2) |* q{+2}{-K} / (|W{-K}(E0)/|W(E0)) and             
154SM2cG |a(M1), |a(E2) and the ratio of electronic factors                     
154SM2cG |W{-K}(E0)/|W(E0) calculated by the code BrIcc                         
154SM cG M(V)      From |a{-K}(exp) in {+154}Pm |b{+-} decay (2.68 m).          
154SM cG M(W)      From |a{-K}(exp) in {+154}Pm |b{+-} decay (1.73 m).          
154SM cG M(T)      From |g(|q) in (|g,|g') (1977Be05) together with the         
154SM2cG      observation that the transition involves a change of parity.      
154SM cG M(U)      From |g(|q) and |g-branching considerations in               
154SM2cG      (|g,|g') (1993Zi05)                                               
154SM cL $In the Inelastic Scattering and (n,n'|g) data sets, a number of levels
154SM2cL are shown which are not included in this Adopted Levels data set. For a
154SM3cL listing of those levels, see those source data sets.                   
154SM cL $2006De19, in (n,n'|g), do not confirm the population of levels at     
154SM2cL 1104, 1120, 1295, 1365 and 1371~keV, if they have J|<5.  see, also, the
154SM3cL Inelastic Scattering Data Set.                                         
154SM cL E         From least-squares fit to |g energies, except omitted are    
154SM2cL  those |g's with questionable placements and E|g's that do not have    
154SM3cL  uncertainties.                                                        
154SM cL E(G)$Proposed as a member of a band by 1992Mo20 in Coul. ex., but the  
154SM2cL existence of the suggested bandhead (at 1371~keV) is questionable, and 
154SM3cL the band characteristics are not otherwise clear.                      
