154SM cL T         The T{-1/2} for two-neutrino double |b{+-} decay to the 2+   
154SM2cL      level in {+154}Gd is measured to be |> 2.3x10{+18} y              
154SM3cL      (1996De60). This is the same value listed in the tabulation of    
154SM4cL      2002Tr04. A model calculation of the T{-1/2} for double           
154SM5cL      |b{+-} decay gives 1.0x10{+23} y for two-neutrino mode and        
154SM5cL      9x10{+24}(m{-n}{+2}) y|*(eV){+2}.                                 
154SM cL           The change in the nuclear charge radius between {+152}Sm     
154SM2cL      and {+154}Sm can given by either |l or |D<r{+2}> where |l =       
154SM3cL      |D<r{+2}> + c{-1} |D<r{+4}> + c{-2} |D<r{+6}>. |l=0.219 fm{+2}    
154SM4cL      {I10} with the corresponding values |D<r{+2}>=0.231 fm{+2}        
154SM5cL      {I11}, |D<r{+4}>=0.00187 fm{+4} {I9}, and |D<r{+6}>=0.0000126     
154SM6cL      fm{+6} {I7} from 1990Wa25. Other values: |l=0.221 {I13}           
154SM7cL      (1973Le16), 0.220 {I11} (1981Ne01) and 0.222 {I11} (1997Ji06)     
154SM8cL      and |D<r{+2}>=0.215 {I16} (1974He28), 0.250 {I14} (1979Po04 as    
154SM8cL      quoted in 1983La06), 0.230 {I12} (1980Br15), 0.230 (1985Al06),    
154SM9cL      0.226 {I12} (1987Bo58), and 0.222 (1990En01). Other: 1989GaZO,    
154SMKcL      1995Ne12, and 1996La03. |D<r{+2}> for the neutron distribution    
154SMScL      is 0.27 {I4} (1983Ja06).                                          
154SM cL           From an analysis of proton-diffraction data using            
154SM2cL      800-MeV protons, 2004Ko34 deduce r{-BS}=5.24 fm {I9} for the      
154SM3cL      "Black-Sphere" radius, taken to be a measure of the matter        
154SM4cL       distribution. The nuclear radius has been reported as            
154SM5cL      <r{+2}>{+1/2}=5.113 fm {I11} (1979Po04) and 5.1143 fm {I9}        
154SM6cL      (1995Fr22 evaluation). From an analysis of data on nuclear rms    
154SM7cL      charge radii, 2004An14 report <r{+2}>{+1/2}=5.111 fm 6, while     
154SM8cL      2007Li14 recommend 5.120 fm 28. For other values, see 1976Co08    
154SM9cL      and 1977HoZF in the (|g,|g'),(e,e') Data Set.                     
