154SM  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154SM dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 28-Aug-2024)          
154SM D  DATA SET UPGRADED (SEPTEMBER, 2007) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE BRICC       
154SM2D   ICC'S, REVISED COMMENTS, AND DIFFERENT ORDERING OF THE PM ISOMERS.    
154SM c  Data are primarily from 1993GrZY, a private communication; any         
154SM2c       conflicts with most complete published sets of data, namely       
154SM3c       1971Da28 and 1974Ya07, are noted. Others:                         
154SM4c       1958Wi42, 1972Ta13, and 1973Pr05.                                 
154SM c  Experimental methods:                                                  
154SM c  1958Wi42, 1960Wi10: Produced by {+154}Sm(n,p). Measured T{-1/2}        
154SM2c      and |b{+-} endpoint, probably for mixture of isomers.              
154SM c  1971Da28: Produced by {+154}Sm(n,p) with enriched (99.5%) target       
154SM2c      and E(n)=14.8 MeV. Measured |g singles, |g|g and |g|b{+-}          
154SM3c      coincidences with NaI and Ge detectors.                            
154SM c  1972Ta13: Produced by {+154}Sm(n,p) with enriched (99.5%) target       
154SM2c      and E(n)=14 MeV. Measured |g singles, |g|g and |g|b{+-}            
154SM3c      coincidences with NaI, Ge, and plastic scintillator detectors.     
154SM c  1973Pr05: Produced by {+154}Sm(n,p) with enriched target and           
154SM2c      E(n)=14.8 MeV. Measured |g and |b{+-} spectra with GM tube, NaI,   
154SM3c      Ge, and Si(Li) detectors.                                          
154SM c  1974Ya07: Produced by {+154}Sm(n,p) with enriched (99.54%) target      
154SM2c      and E(n) |? 15 MeV. Measured |g singles and |g|g coincidences      
154SM3c      with NaI and Ge detectors.                                         
154SM c  1990Ba57: Produced by {+252}Cf spontaneous fission with radiochemistry.
154SM2c       Level scheme only, no |g data included. See 1993GrZY.             
154SM c  1993GrZY: Produced by {+252}Cf spontaneous fission with isotope        
154SM2c       separation. Measured |g singles and |g|g coincidences.            
154SM3c       Private communication.                                            
154SM c  1995Gr19: Produced by {+252}Cf spontaneous fission with isotope        
154SM2c       separation. Measured I|b(0+82) with a 4|p|b|g system.             
154SM c  1997Gr09: Produced by {+252}Cf spontaneous fission with isotope        
154SM2c       separation. Measured I|b{+-} as a function excitation energy with 
154SM3c       a total absorption |g spectrometer.                               
154SM cB $The I|b{+-} to the excited levels have been deduced independently of  
154SM2cB the |g data from the total absorption |g spectrometer, TAGS, data of   
154SM3cB 1997Gr09. The measured spectrum represents approximately the |b{+-}    
154SM4cB feeding intensity as a function of the excitation energy. When         
154SM5cB necessary, new levels, called "pseudolevels", and associated decay |g's
154SM6cB are included in the analysis.  Since the resolution of the TAGS system 
154SM7cB is typically 50-100~keV, the intensity assigned to a pseudolevel may   
154SM8cB represent the |b{+-} feeding to a single level or to a group of levels 
154SM9cB in that region.                                                        
154SM cB IB        Values are from |g intensity balances, except those for      
154SM2cB      the 0- and 82-keV levels which are from measurements of 1995Gr19. 
154SM3cB      The quoted uncertainties do not include any contribution from     
154SM4cB      the possible placement of the unplaced |g's.                      
154SM5cB      The I|b{+-} values from the TAGS data (1997Gr09) are generally    
154SM6cB      in excellent agreement with those from the intensity balances.    
154SM7cB      The TAGS value is given in a comment if it differs by more        
154SM8cB      than 10%. Since the decay scheme is not complete, values          
154SM9cB      below 0.2% are not given.                                         
154SM cB IB        The pseudolevels and the associated I|b{+-} from the TAGS    
154SM2cB      data analysis are 3300 keV, 0.36%; 3400, 0.45; 3500, 0.45; 3600,  
154SM3cB      0.112; 3700, 0.134; 3800, 0.038; and 3900, 0.013.                 
154SM cG E         From 1993GrZY. Others: 1974Ya07, 1971Da28.                   
154SM cG E         Unplaced |g's are from 1993GrZY. Others: 1974Ya07, but some  
154SM2cG      of these |g's are placed by 1993GrZY; also 1971Da28, but they     
154SM3cG      are not assigned to a specific isomer.                            
154SM cG RI        From 1993GrZY. Other: 1974Ya07.                              
154SM cG RI        I(Kx|a)=16.9 and I(Kx|b)=4.4                                 
154SM cG M$Adopted values. Some values were measured in this dataset from       
154SM4cG measured |a{-K}(exp) values obtained from I(K x ray) and I|g           
154SM4cG ratios (1993GrZY, with the |a{-K}(exp) values given in comments)       
154SM cG E(R)      Existence and placement of |g are uncertain                  
154SM cL E         From least-squares fit to |g energies, except |g's with      
154SM2cL      questionable placements are omitted.                              
154SM cL J         From {+154}Sm Adopted Levels.                                
154SM CL BAND(A)$K{+|p}=0+ ground state band.                                   
154SM CL BAND(B)$K{+|p}=0- octupole-vibrational band.                           
154SM CL BAND(C)$First excited K{+|p}=0+ band.                                  
