154SM    INELASTIC SCATTERING          1968VE01,1964KE08         25NDS    202503
154SM  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154SM D  DATA SET UPDATED (OCTOBER, 2007) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE COMMENTS       
154SM2D   REGARDING THE NON-ADOPTION OF CERTAIN LEVELS REPORTED IN THIS DATA    
154SM3D   SET.                                                                  
154SM c  Several levels listed here are not included in the Adopted Levels.     
154SM2c  Some are not confirmed in the most recent (n,n'|g) study, where they   
154SM3c  should have been seen if their J{+|p} values were |<5.                 
154SM c  The studies that provide level-structure information are: for (p,p'),  
154SM2c       1961Co27, 1964Ke08 and 1990Fr07; and, for (d,d'): 1965Ze01,       
154SM3c       1966El07 and 1968Ve01, with E(p) or E(d)=12 MeV.                  
154SM c  A large number of other studies of inelastic scattering have been      
154SM2c       made for a variety of purposes. These include moments:            
154SM3c       1982An10, 1982Cl03, 1983Ro11, 1986Ic02, and 1989Gu09; nuclear     
154SM4c       shapes: 1970Ap03, 1972Yu03, 1973SaXO, 1977Mc02, 1980DeYV,         
154SM5c       1987Ic04, 1989Gu09, and 1989Ob02; angular distribution of         
154SM6c       outgoing particle: 1966Ze03, 1967Ha05, 1968He24, 1970Br19,        
154SM7c       1970Fu05, 1972Wo03, 1975Ea03, 1975La18, 1977Ea01, 1979Ki14,       
154SM8c       1979Pa08, 1980Ba30, 1987Ic01, 1989Gu09, and 1989Ob02; spin        
154SM9c       contribution to excitation of collective 1+ level: 1985Dj02       
154SM0c       and 1990Fr07; and others: 1967Ku14, 1967St09, 1971FuZV,           
154SMAc       1971Kr10, 1972Ku15, 1975Ea01, 1980La18, 1981Am03, 1981An04,       
154SMBc       1981Ra10, 1983Ha16, 1983Oh02, and 1983Pa08.                       
154SM c  Experimental methods:                                                  
154SM c  1961Co27: (p,p') with E(p)=11 MeV. Report 2 excited states.            
154SM D  1963Ke07, 1963Ke12: See 1964Ke08.                                      
154SM c  1964Ke08: (p,p') on enriched (99.07%) target with E(p)=12 MeV.         
154SM2c       p' measured in magnetic spectrometer at five angles. Report       
154SM3c       22 levels.                                                        
154SM c  1965Ze01: (d,d') on enriched (99%) target with E(d)=12 MeV. d'         
154SM2c       measured with Si(Au) detector telescope, and magnetic             
154SM3c       spectrometer. Confirms J|p of several states.                     
154SM c  1966El07: (d,d') on enriched target with E(d)=12 MeV. d' measured      
154SM2c       in magnetic spectrometer. Report relative population of           
154SM3c       ground-state band members.                                        
154SM D  1966Ze03: (d,d') on enriched (AP 99%) target with E(d)=12 MeV. d'      
154SM2D       measured with Si(Au) detectors and magnetic spectrograph.         
154SM3D       d(THETA) measured for levels of different JPI. Report 5 levels    
154SM4D       in table and 11 in figure.                                        
154SM D  1967Ha05: (A,A'). Measured differential cross sections of 3 levels.    
154SM D  1967Ku14: (p,p'). Discuss use of reaction. Sees 7 levels.              
154SM D  1967St09: (p,p'). Study of reaction properties. See 3 levels.          
154SM D  1968He24: (A,A'). Measured differential cross sections of 3 levels.    
154SM c  1968Ve01: (d,d') on enriched (>96%) target with E(d)=12.1 MeV. d'      
154SM2c      measured in magnetic spectrograph at four angles. FMHM=15-20 and   
154SM3c      7-10 keV. J|p from ratios of cross sections at 90|' and 125|'.     
154SM4c      Report 21 levels. See also Coulomb excitation data set.            
154SM D  1970Ap03: (A,A'). Study of nuclear shapes.                             
154SM D  1970ApZZ: See 1970Ap03.                                                
154SM D  1970Br19: (p,p') with E(p)=16 MeV. Reanalysis of earlier (1967St09)    
154SM2D       data and deduced deformation parameters.                          
154SM D  1970Fu05: (p,p'). Measured differential cross section.                 
154SM D  1971BrYM: (A,A') with EA=10-18 MeV. See 1974Br31.                      
154SM D  1971FuZV: (p,p') with E(p)=50.8 MeV. Study of reaction mechanism.      
154SM D  1971Kr10: (p,p') with E(p)=16 MeV. Study of reaction mechanism.        
154SM D  1972KuZJ: See 1972Ku15.                                                
154SM D  1972Ku15: (p,p') with E(p)=12 MeV. Study of reaction mechanism.        
154SM D  1972Wo03: (p,p') with E(p)=50.8 MeV. Measured diff. cross section.     
154SM D  1972Yu03: (A,A'). Study of nuclear shape.                              
154SM D  1973CoWN: (A,A'). Calculated interference effects.                     
154SM D  1973PaZI, 1973PeZN, 1973PeZR: See 1974Pa04.                            
154SM D  1973SaXO: (A,A') with EA=11-13 MeV. Study of nuclear shape.            
154SM D  1973StZH: (A,A'). No structure data.                                   
154SM D  1973WoZE:  See 1977Wo03.                                               
154SM D  1974BeYJ: (A,A') with EA=11-21 MeV. Same information as 1973BeZO.      
154SM D  1974BeYO:  See 1978Be55 and 1979Be04.                                  
154SM D  1974ClZS, 1974EaZY: See 1975Ea01 and 1975Ea03.                         
154SM D  1974Pa04: (3He,3He') with E(3He)=40.9 MeV. No structure data.          
154SM D  1975Ea01: (3He,3He'). Measured diff. cross section.                    
154SM D  1975Ea03: (3He,3He'). Calculations.                                    
154SM D  1975WeZG: (16O,16O') with E(16O)=20-67 MeV. See three states.          
154SM D  1976LeZY: (A,A'). No structure data.                                   
154SM D  1977Ea01: (3He,3He') with E(3He)=53.4 MeV. Measured diff. cross sectio 
154SM D  1978GaZM: (6Li,6Li') with E(6Li)=75 MeV. Not used.                     
154SM D  1978Mo10: (A,A') with EA=115 MeV.                                      
154SM D  1979Ki14: (p,p') on enriched (99%) target with E(p)=35 MeV. p'(THETA)  
154SM2D       measured in magnetic spectrometer for 2+, 4+, 6+, and 8+ levels.  
154SM D  1979Pa08: (3He,3He') on highly enriched target with E(3He)=40.9 MeV.   
154SM2D       3HE(THETA) measured for 0+, 2+, 4+, and 6+ levels.                
154SM D  1980Ba30: (p,p') on enriched (98.69%) target with E(p)=800 MeV.        
154SM2D   p'(THETA) measured for 0+, 2+, 4+, and 6+ levels.                     
154SM D  1980Ga21: (A,A') with EA=96, 129 MeV. No structure data.               
154SM D  1980GaZV:  See 1980Ga21.                                               
154SM D  1981Am03: (p,p'). Calculated reaction properties.                      
154SM D  1981Ra10: (p,p') with E(p)=800 MeV. Study of reaction properties.      
