154SM c  The level energies and |g data are from 2006De19, who report |?205     
154SM2c  |g's. Others: 1986Be52, who report|?165 |g's; 1973El09, who report|?35 
154SM3c  |g's; 1978Si13, who report 6 |g's; and 1996Ko41, who report level      
154SM4c  populations. The level lifetimes are from 1993Ju04.                    
154SM c  2006De19 report detailed information on levels only up to|?1.99~MeV.   
154SM2c  these authors give much less detailed information on levels above this 
154SM3c  energy. In a number of cases, these levels lead to the emission of only
154SM4c  1 or 2 |g's. In such cases, these levels generally are not included as 
154SM5c  (n,n'|g) levels in the Adopted Levels.                                 
154SM c  2006De19 do not confirm the population in (n,n'|g) of levels at 1104,  
154SM2c  1120, 1295, 1365 and 1371~keV, if they have J|<5. Also, they do not    
154SM3c  confirm the population of the 1577~keV, 6+ member of the first excited 
154SM4c  K{+|p}=0+ band and the 2154.3~keV, 7+ member of the |g band, which were
154SM5c  reported in an earlier (n,n'|g) study.                                 
154SM c  2006De19: enriched (97.9%) target of mass 10 g and thickness 0.58      
154SM2c  g/cm{+2} irradiated in a beam of fast-reactor neutrons. |g's detected  
154SM3c  using a HPGe detector of efficiency 10% and FWHM 2.4~keV at 1.3~MeV. |g
154SM4c  spectra measured at angles of 90, 105, 115, 125, 135, 142 and 150|'    
154SM5c  with respect to the beam direction. Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q). Report  
154SM6c  level scheme and |d values for many of the |g's.                       
154SM c  1986Be52: Enriched (98.5%) target with reactor neutrons.               
154SM c  1996Ko41: reactor neutrons.                                            
154SM c  1993Ju04: E(n)=1.3 MeV on natural Sm target. Doppler-shift             
154SM2c      attenuation method, spectra measured at eight angles between 35|'  
154SM3c      and 144|'.                                                         
154SM c  1978Si13: E(n)=2.75 MeV.                                               
154SM c  1973El09: Enriched (99.54%) target; n from p bombardment of {+7}Li     
154SM2c      and maximum n energies of 1.1 to 2.3 MeV.                          
