154SM  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154SM D  DATA SET UPDATED (OCTOBER, 2007) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE NEW DATA,      
154SM2D   CHANGE ADOPTION OF A BAND, AND REVISE SOME COMMENTS.                  
154SM c  2012Mo23 compiled for XUNDL database by B. Singh (McMaster)            
154SM c  2014Sm02 compiled for XUNDL database by A. M. Hurst (LBNL)             
154SM c  There have been numerous Coulomb excitation measurements. Those        
154SM2c       giving electric moments are: 1960Ad01, 1960El07, 1961Go09,        
154SM3c       1963Gr04, 1964Al25, 1964Ho25, 1965Yo04, 1966Se06, 1968Ke04,       
154SM4c       1969Fr11, 1971St24, 1972Sa42, 1973Be40, 1973Eb01, 1974Br31,       
154SM5c       1974Sh12, 1974Wo01, 1976Co08, 1977Fi01, 1977Wo03, and 1979Ki14;   
154SM6c       magnetic moments: 1958Go72, 1967Wo06, 1968Be42, 1969Wh04,         
154SM7c       1970Be36, 1971Ku09, 1972Ku10, 1974Ar23, and 1975Ro24; lifetime    
154SM8c       studies:  1959Bi10, 1967Wo06, 1968Ri09, 1972Di06, 1977Ke06,       
154SM9c       1980Jo08, and 1999Kr10; levels: 1992Mo20 and 1999As05; and        
154SM0c       other studies: 1962Af01, 1964De07, 1966El07, 1968Br03,            
154SMAc       1968Ve01, and 1970Da28.                                           
154SM D  References not used because they are abstracts, reports that are       
154SM2D      preliminary, have been superseded, or repeat earlier results       
154SM3D      are: 1958Ch36, 1963De31 (see 1964De07), 1963Se01 (see 1966Se06),   
154SM4D      1964Yo01, 1969WhZZ (see 1969Wh04), 1971StZJ (see 1971St24),        
154SM5D      1972BrYV, 1972MuZK, 1973BeZO (see 1973Be40), 1973Da03, 1973GrXL,   
154SM6D      1973StYX and 1974StZI (see 1980Jo08), 1974ShYS (see 1974Sh12),     
154SM7D      (see 1980Jo08), 1975Le22 (see 1973Be40), 1977HoZF, and 2001KuZU.   
154SM c  A number of the studies listed here report measurements of |m and Q    
154SM2c  values for several {+154}Sm levels. These data are not listed here, but
154SM3c  are summarized in the Adopted Levels data set for the respective level.
154SM c  Experimental methods:                                                  
154SM c  1958Ch36: Natural Sm target, p beam with E|<3.7 MeV. E|g(82)           
154SM2c       measured with curved-crystal spectrometer.                        
154SM c  1958Go72: p beam with E(p)=2.1 MeV. Measured perturbed |g(|q) with     
154SM2c       NaI detectors to determine g-factor.                              
154SM c  1959Bi10: Natural Sm target, pulsed p beam with E(p)=2.8 MeV. |g       
154SM2c       measured with plastic scintillator. Report T{-1/2}(82).           
154SM c  1960Ad01: Natural Sm target, {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=36, 39 MeV.    
154SM2c       |g measured with NaI detector, two states observed.               
154SM c  1960El07: p and d beams with E=4.5 MeV. Magnetic spectrograph.         
154SM2c       Report B(E2)(82).                                                 
154SM c  1961Go09: p beam. Measured thick target yields, report B(E2)(82).      
154SM c  1962Af01: Measured yields.                                             
154SM c  1963Gr04: Enriched target, {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=14-50 MeV. ce    
154SM2c       measured in magnetic spectrometer, report E for 4+ level.         
154SM c  1964Al25: Enriched target, {+14}N beam with E({+14}N)=37 MeV. Report   
154SM2c       B(E2)(2+|)4+).                                                    
154SM c  1964De07: Enriched target, {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)|<44 MeV.         
154SM2c       Scattered {+16}O counted in solid-state counter and |g in NaI     
154SM3c       detector. Measured level population probabilities.                
154SM c  1964Ho25: {+14}N beam with E({+14}N)=11.0 MeV. |g measured with NaI    
154SM2c       detector, report B(E2)(82).                                       
154SM c  1965Yo04: Natural and enriched (99.07%) targets, {+16}O beam with      
154SM2c       E(16{+}O)=43.5 MeV. |g measured with NaI and particles with       
154SM3c       Si(Au) detectors, report B(E2)(1180,1440).                        
154SM c  1966El07: Enriched target, d beam with E(d)=12 MeV. Magnetic           
154SM2c       spectrometer, report relative population of states.               
154SM c  1966Se06: Enriched (> 99%) target, {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)|<65 MeV. 
154SM2c       |g measured with NaI detectors in singles, |g|g, and |g-particle  
154SM3c       coincidence modes, report B(E3)(1012).                            
154SM c  1967Wo06: Enriched (> 96%) target, pulsed p beam. Measured T{-1/2}     
154SM2c       and g factor from precession of |g angular distribution.          
154SM c  1968Be42: Enriched target, {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=36 MeV.          
154SM2c       Recoil-into-gas technique used to deduce g-factor(82).            
154SM c  1968Br03: Recoil nuclei implanted in polarized magnetic environment    
154SM2c       and measured precession of |g angular distribution.               
154SM c  1968Ke04: Additional analysis of data used in 1965Yo04. Report         
154SM2c       B(E3)(1012).                                                      
154SM c  1968Ri09: Pulsed proton beam, E(p)=3.5 MeV.                            
154SM2c       |g measured with NaI, report T{-1/2}(82).                         
154SM c  1968Ve01: (d,d') with E(d)=12.1 MeV and (|a,|a') with E(|a)=16.1 MeV.  
154SM2c       Measured level energies and |g(|q).                               
154SM c  1969Fr11: {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=48-60 MeV and {+32}S beam with    
154SM2c       E({+32}S)=86.7-110 MeV. |g measured with Ge detector in           
154SM3c       coincidence with the scattered projectiles, report B(E2)(82).     
154SM c  1969Wh04: Mossbauer measurement. Report magnetic moment.               
154SM c  1970Be36: Reevaluation of g-factor of 1968Be42.                        
154SM c  1970Da28: Enriched (99.88%) target, {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=33 MeV. 
154SM2c       Measured ce's in magnetic spectrometer, report multipolarity      
154SM3c       of |g(82,185).                                                    
154SM c  1971Ku09: {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=52 MeV. Measured perturbed        
154SM2c       |g(|q), report g-factors of 4+ and 6+ states.                     
154SM c  1971St24: Natural Sm target, |a beam with E(|a)=10-12 MeV. Report E4   
154SM2c       matrix element.                                                   
154SM c  1972Di06: {+40}Ar beam with E({+40}Ar)=146 MeV. |g measured with Ge    
154SM2c       detector.                                                         
154SM2c       T{-1/2}(4+,6+,8+) measured by recoil-distance Doppler-shift       
154SM3c       method.                                                           
154SM c  1972Ku10: {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=35 MeV. Measured perturbed        
154SM2c       |g(|q). Report g-factor(4+,6+).                                   
154SM c  1972Sa42: |a beam with E(|a)=10.5-12 MeV. |a measured in Si(Au)        
154SM2c       detector and magnetic spectrometer. Report B(E2)(82) and E4       
154SM3c       matrix element.                                                   
154SM c  1973Be40: Enriched target, |a beam with E(|a)=11.0-21.0 MeV. |a        
154SM2c       measured in magnetic spectrometer. Report E2 and E4 matrix        
154SM3c       elements.                                                         
154SM c  1973Eb01: Enriched (99%) target, |a beam with E(|a)=12 MeV, {+16}O     
154SM2c       beam with E({+16}O)=24-30 MeV, and {+32}S beam with               
154SM3c       E({+32}S)=35-40 MeV. |g measured using a Ge detector.             
154SM4c       Report E4 matrix element.                                         
154SM c  1974Br31: Enriched (99.8%) target, |a beam with E(|a)=11-20 MeV. |a    
154SM2c       measured with Si(Au) detectors. Report E2 and E4 matrix elements. 
154SM c  1974Sh12: |a beam with E(|a)=8-17 MeV. |a measured in Si(Au) detector. 
154SM2c       Report B(E2)(82) and E4 matrix element.                           
154SM c  1974Wo01: Enriched target, |a beam with E(|a)=12 MeV. |a measured in   
154SM2c       Si(Au) detector. Report E2 and E4 matrix elements.                
154SM c  1975Le22: |a beam with E(|a)=12-19 MeV. |a measured in magnetic        
154SM2c       spectrometer. See 1973Be40 for same results.                      
154SM c  1975Ro24: {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=40 MeV. Measured |g|g(|q).        
154SM c  1977Fi01: Enriched (98.69%) target, |a beam with E(|a)=11.23-12.00 MeV.
154SM2c       |a measured in Si(Au) detector. Report E2 and E4 matrix elements. 
154SM c  1977Ke06: Enriched target, {+56}Fe and {+84}Kr beams with E=4.14       
154SM2c       MeV/nucleon. |g measured with Ge detector. T{-1/2}(8+,10+,12+)    
154SM3c       determined by Doppler-broadened lineshape method.                 
154SM c  1977Wo03: Enriched target, |a beam with E(|a)=11.5-12 MeV. Si(Au)      
154SM2c       detector. Report B(E2)(82).                                       
154SM c  1979Ki14: Enriched (94%) target, p beam with E(p)=35 MeV. Measured     
154SM2c       p' measured in magnetic spectrometer. Report E2 and E4 moments.   
154SM c  1980Jo08: {+40}Ar beam with E({+40}Ar)=146,153 MeV. |g's measured with 
154SM2c       Ge(Li) detector. T{-1/2}(4+,6+,8+,10+) determined by              
154SM3c       Doppler-shift recoil-distance method.                             
154SM c  1992Mo20: {+58}Ni beam with E({+58}Ni)=220 MeV. |g's measured with     
154SM2c       array of 20 Ge detectors and recoil {+58}Ni with 5 Si detectors.  
154SM3c       Measured coincidences and |g(|q), report 5 bands with J|p to 16+, 
154SM4c       13-, 6+, 14+, and 7+. Report only level energies, no E|g or I|g.  
154SM c  1999As05: {+176}Yb and {+208}Pb beams, measured |g's with GAMMASPHERE  
154SM2c       array of 55 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors. Report levels        
154SM3c       in ground-state band up to 22+.                                   
154SM c  1999Kr10: {+16}O beam with E({+16}O)=65 MeV. Measured |g's in YRAST    
154SM2c       Ball array of 3 Clover detectors, 19 Compton-shielded Ge          
154SM3c       detectors and particles with 8 photoelectric cells. Measured      
154SM4c       T{-1/2} by Doppler-shifted Attenuation Method (DSAM) for 3 levels.
154SM c  2000KuZT: {+90}Zr beam, E({+90}Zr)=380~MeV. Enriched target, |g's      
154SM2c  detected in the GEMINI Ge-detector array. Show only two gated |g-ray   
154SM3c  spectra. Present only |g's within the g.s. band. g.s. band mentioned   
154SM4c  only up to the 16+ member.                                             
154SM c  2001MoZT: {+90}Zr beam, E({+90}Zr)=340~MeV. Discuss relative population
154SM2c  in Coul. ex. of the members of the first two excited K{+|p}=0+ bands.  
154SM3c  Many of the same authors as 2000KuZT.                                  
154SM c  2009WiZU: {+154}Sm({+16}O,{+16}O'), E=55, 60, 65 MeV; measured         
154SM2c  conversion electrons Ee, Ie after Coulomb excitation; deduced monopole 
154SM2c  strength, |b-band                                                      
154SM c  2012Mo23: E=570 MeV {+154}Sm beam from Atlas accelerator at ANL on     
154SM2c  0.63 mg/cm{+2} {+12}C target. Gamma rays                               
154SM2c  detected by Gammasphere array of 99 HPGe detectors. Measured           
154SM3c  E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g(|q). Deduced E2 matrix elements from analysis of    
154SM2c  relative Coul. ex. yields with a multiple Coulomb excitation code based
154SM3c  on Winther-de Boer theory. Matrix elements were constrained by the     
154SM4c  experimental branching ratios and multipole mixing ratios. Known       
154SM5c  B(E2) values for g.s. band transitions and known static quadrupole     
154SM6c  moments for the first 2+ and 4+ states were included in the analysis.  
154SM7c  Relative sign of E2 matrix elements were derived from Alaga rule.      
154SM8c  Comparison with X(5) and CBS model calculations                        
154SM c  2014Sm02: E=65 MeV {+16}O beam on 1.5 mg/cm{+2} thick 99% enriched     
154SM3c  {+154}Sm target. Measured |g rays and ce due to Coulomb excitation of  
154SM4c  {+154}Sm using Silicon And GErmanium (SAGE) spectrometer at the        
154SM5c  University of Jyv~askyl~a composed of 34 High-Purity Germanium (HPGe)  
154SM6c  detectors (24 clovers and 10 EUROGAM Phase I detectors) from the       
154SM7c  JUROGAMII array coupled to a 1-mm thick 90-segment single-sided        
154SM8c  annular silicon strip detector. Data collected for 65 h using          
154SM9c  with average beam current of 20 pnA.                                   
154SMAc  Measured |g-|g and |g-ce coincidences. Deduced levels, E{-|g},         
154SMBc  K-conversion coefficient and multipolarities. Electric monopole        
154SMCc  transition strengths determined and compared to Bohr and Mottelson     
154SMDc  |b-vibrational model, the Interacting Boson Model (IBA), and two-state 
154SMEc  mixing calculations. Low values for measured monopole strength         
154SMFc  inconsistent with a |b-vibrational mode.                               
