154EU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154EU dG $Transition strength is calculated by Java-RULER (version 08-Feb-2024) 
154EU  Q 1968.0    8 6442.22 24 6467.3 7 -566    20    2021WA16                 
154EU cQ $S(2n)=14992.50 {I27}, S(2p)=15062 {I26} (2021Wa16)                    
154EU c  These data are primarily from (n,|g) studies (1987Ba52 and 1978PrZY),  
154EU2c       with some information from {+154}Eu (46 min) isomeric decay       
154EU3c       (1975Ca22, 1976Ch08, and 1976Zo01), in-beam |g studies            
154EU4c       (1988Ka01 and 1980Be61), {+153}Eu(d,p) studies (1987Ba52), and    
154EU5c       {+154}Eu(p,p') (1979La11).                                        
154EU c  Model and theory articles of interest:                                 
154EU2c       configurations - 1984Ro06, 1987Ba52; bandhead energies, band      
154EU3c       mixing, splitting of Gallagher-Moszkowski doublets, and           
154EU4c       configurations - 1987Gu19; discuss the rotational bands           
154EU5c       in terms of parity doublets and thus of octupole deformation      
154EU6c       - 1989Sh08; octupole deformation - 1990Af03.                      
154EU cG           Primary |g's from (n,|g) are not included here;              
154EU2cG      see the {+153}Eu(n,|g) data sets for this information.            
154EU cG           Unplaced |g's are not given here; see {+153}Eu(n,|g) and     
154EU2cG      {+154}Sm({+3}He,p2n|g).                                           
154EU cG E         Most values are from the (n,|g) study of 1987Ba52; other     
154EU2cG      sets of values are given by 1977St14 and by Shera, as quoted in   
154EU3cG      1968Gr32.                                                         
154EU cG M,MR      From 1987Ba52, unless otherwise noted. The results of        
154EU2cG      1987Ba52 are assumed to replace those of 1978PrZY and 1977St14.   
154EU3cG      Many of the assignments of 1977St14 appear to differ from those   
154EU4cG      of 1987Ba52, but this may result from the inability to resolve    
154EU5cG      closely spaced peaks in the study of 1977St14. 1976Ch08, in       
154EU6cG      IT decay, contribute some results.                                
154EU cL           The (n,|g) studies of 1987Ba52 include resonance-averaged n  
154EU2cL    capture with a 2-keV beam. These authors state that they have       
154EU3cL    observed: (1) all of the levels with 1 |< J |< 6 below 300 keV;     
154EU4cL    (2) all of the 1-, 2-, 3-, and 4- levels up to about 450 keV; and   
154EU5cL    (3) most of the 1+, 2+, 3+, and 4+ levels from 300 to 450 keV.      
154EU cL           Band parameters are given for several bands; for many        
154EU2cL      other bands the parameters are unusual and presumably reflect     
154EU3cL      the influence of strong coupling among bands.                     
154EU cL $Listed configurations are the dominant ones. Some levels may contain  
154EU2cL sizable admixtures of other configurations.                            
154EU cL E         The best value from the individual excitation modes; those   
154EU2cL      from the (n,|g) study are from a least-squares fit to |g          
154EU3cL      energies as quoted by 1987Ba52.                                   
154EU cL J         1987Ba52 give a detailed discussion of the model-independent 
154EU2cL      arguments for most of the J|p assignments included here, as well  
154EU3cL      as the model-dependent arguments for the J|p, band, and           
154EU4cL      configuration assignments. These assignments are based on: (1)    
154EU5cL      measured |g multipolarities; (2) the existence of rotational      
154EU6cL      bands and the configurations that are expected to occur at low    
154EU7cL      energy; and (3) the completeness of the set of observed levels.   
154EU8cL      These J|p arguments are not always listed here and should be      
154EU9cL      referred to by the interested reader.                             
154EU cL J         In a number of cases, the J|p assignments from the (n,|g)    
154EU2cL      study (1987Ba52) are not unique. In these instances, where the    
154EU3cL      band structure seems well established (i.e., at least three       
154EU4cL      levels observed), the evaluator has used band-structure           
154EU5cL      considerations to select from the possibilities only one value.   
154EU6cL      These spins are generally shown in parentheses.                   
154EU cL T         From (n,|g) by 1984Ro06, unless otherwise noted.             
