154EU    153EU(N,G) E=TH               1987BA52,1978PRZY,1984RO0625NDS    202503
154EU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154EU D  DATA SET UPDATED (JANUARY, 2008) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE ICC DATA,      
154EU2D  REVISED AND EXPANDED COMMENTS, CHANGING THE LISTING OF SOME BANDS,     
154EU3D  AND SOME MODIFICATIONS OF THE JPI'S.                                   
154EU c  These data are from 1987Ba52, unless otherwise noted; this article     
154EU2c       includes some or all of the data presented by the authors of      
154EU3c       1978PrZY, 1977St14, and 1978PrZK, so the evaluator assumes that   
154EU4c       the data of 1987Ba52 replace the corresponding data of these      
154EU5c       earlier articles. The internal-conversion data are given in       
154EU6c       more detail in 1978PrZY; and the primary |g data are given        
154EU7c       explicitly only in 1978PrZY. 1987Ba52 give results for            
154EU8c       thermal-neutron capture, resonance-averaged capture with 2-keV    
154EU9c       neutrons, and resonance capture at 2.4 and 3.3 eV; the latter     
154EU0c       data are given in other data sets in this evaluation. Level       
154EUAc       half-lives are given by 1984Ro06.                                 
154EUBc       Other (n,|g) results are given by 1960Sc05, 1963Or02, 1964Be41,   
154EUCc       1966Ne06, 1967Bo30, 1968Gr32, 1969MuZM, 1975StZI (see 1977St14),  
154EUDc       and 1977PrZT (see 1978PrZY).                                      
154EU c  Experimental methods:                                                  
154EU c  1960Sc05:  Probably thermal-n capture in normal Eu. Measured E|g       
154EU2c      and I|g with curved-crystal spectrometer; report 10 |g's,          
154EU3c      mostly in {+152}Eu.                                                
154EU c  1963Or02:  Thermal-n capture in enriched (95%) sample. Measured        
154EU2c      E|g and I|g with curved-crystal spectrometer; report 9 |g's.       
154EU c  1964Be41:  Thermal-n capture in enriched sample. Measured |g's         
154EU2c      with NaI(Tl) detectors; report 2 level lifetimes from |g|g and     
154EU3c      x|g coin.                                                          
154EU c  1966Ne06:  Measured I|g curved-crystal spectrometer; report 4 |g's.    
154EU c  1967Bo30:  Capture in enriched (98.9% and 1.8%) samples. Measured      
154EU2c      ce in magnetic spectrograph with FWHM=0.4% with |? 50%             
154EU3c      uncertainty on intensities; report |? 50 |g's.                     
154EU c  1975StZI:  Abstract only.  See 1977St14.                               
154EU c  1977St14:  Capture in enriched (99.1%) sample. Measured ce             
154EU2c       with magnetic spectrometer and |g's at low energies               
154EU3c       with Si(Li) and Ge detectors and at high energies with a pair     
154EU4c       spectrometer based on a Ge detector. Measured |g|g coincidences   
154EU5c       and lifetimes by |g|g(t).                                         
154EU c  1978PrZY:  Same measurement methods as 1987Ba52. Also, abstracts       
154EU2c       and summary by same authors: 1977PrZT, 1978PrZJ, and 1978PrZK     
154EU c  1984Ro06:  Capture in enriched (99.1%) target. Measured lifetimes      
154EU2c       by delayed |g|g(t) with Ge detector and plastic scintillator.     
154EU c  1987Ba52:  Capture at ILL reactor. Measured ce with magnetic           
154EU2c       spectrometer (FWHM=0.03% at 200 keV) and |g's with                
154EU3c       curved-crystal spectrometers (FWHM |< 0.1 keV at 100 keV)         
154EU4c       below 1500 keV and with pair spectrometer above this energy.      
154EU cG E         From 1987Ba52 for |g's from levels below 600 keV and from    
154EU2cG      1978PrZY for |g's from the capture state, unless otherwise        
154EU3cG      noted. The uncertainties in E|g from 1987Ba52 do not include      
154EU4cG      a calibration uncertainty of 1 part in 10{+5}. Other sets of      
154EU5cG      E|g: 1977St14 from semiconductor detectors and 1963Or02 and       
154EU6cG      1969MuZM from curved-crystal spectrometers.                       
154EU cG RI        From 1987Ba52 for |g's from levels below 600 keV and from    
154EU2cG      1978PrZY for |g's from the capture state, unless otherwise        
154EU3cG      noted.                                                            
154EU cG M,MR      From {+154}Eu Adopted |g radiations, but primarily from      
154EU2cG      these (n,|g) studies and based on L-subshell ratios and           
154EU3cG      |a{-K}(exp) and |a{-L}(exp) values (1987Ba52 and 1978PrZY).       
154EU4cG      Other: 1977St14.                                                  
154EU cG E(U),RI(U)$From 1977St14.                                              
154EU cG RI(Z)     1987Ba52 indicate possible double placement, but the other   
154EU2cG      placement is not given.                                           
154EU cG M(T)      Reported as E1 or E2                                         
154EU cL $For a listing of the configuration assignments for the various bands, 
154EU2cL see the Adopted Levels data set. These assignments are those proposed  
154EU3cL by 1987Ba52.                                                           
154EU cL E         From 1987Ba52 for levels below 600 keV. For levels above     
154EU2cL      600 keV, energies are computed from thermal-neutron capture       
154EU3cL      state energy of 6442.2 keV and the primary |g energy from         
154EU4cL      1978PrZY.                                                         
154EU cL J         From 1987Ba52 and based on |g multipolarities, |g            
154EU2cL      intensities in resonance-average n capture, and band structure.   
154EU3cL      The conclusions from resonance-averaged capture are not given     
154EU4cL      explicitly by the authors but were taken into consideration in    
154EU5cL      arriving at their J|p assignments. The J|p's in the Adopted       
154EU6cL      Levels differ in some ways because they are based on the          
154EU7cL      specific arguments given there. The (n,|g) level-scheme table     
154EU8cL      (table 3) and the summary of levels from all the data (table 4)   
154EU9cL      of 1987Ba52 give slightly different J|p assignments; those        
154EUKcL      quoted here are generally from this latter table in 1987Ba52.     
154EU cL T         From 1984Ro06, unless otherwise noted. These are from (n,|g) 
154EU2cL      only. See Adopted Levels for results from all measurements.       
