154EU2c   (n,|g) work of 1984Ro06. The |g data are from 1980Be61 and 1988Ka21.  
154EU c  1988Ka01: {+154}Sm({+3}He,p2n|g), E({+3}He)=22 to 27 MeV and           
154EU2c     (d,2n|g), E(d)=10 MeV. Only those |g's placed in the scheme         
154EU3c     are reported. No I|g values are reported, and only a general        
154EU4c     statement of the uncertainties in the |g energies                   
154EU5c     (0.1 to 0.2 keV) is given.                                          
154EU c  1980Be61: {+154}Sm(d,2n|g), E(d)=13.5 MeV and (p,n|g), E(p)=6.7 MeV.   
154EU2c   No |g placements given, but E|g and I|g are given with uncertainties  
154EU3c   for both reactions.                                                   
154EU cG           Unplaced |g's are from 1980Be61.                             
154EU cG           Coincidence relationships are from 1988Ka01.                 
154EU cG E         Values with uncertainties are from 1980Be61 with placement   
154EU2cG     by evaluator, all other values and placements are from 1988Ka01.   
154EU cG RI        From (d,2n|g) at 13.5 MeV (1980Be61). Values without         
154EU2cG      uncertainties have had a contribution from {+153}Eu               
154EU3cG      subtracted.                                                       
154EU cG RI(W)     Value may include contribution from {+153}Eu.                
154EU cL E         Where evaluator has placed |g's from 1980Be61, the level     
154EU2cL      energies are from a least-squares fit to the |g energies;         
154EU3cL      otherwise, they are from 1988Ka01. From the general comments of   
154EU4cL      1988Ka01, the latter level energies are probably accurate to      
154EU5cL      about 0.1 keV; however, no uncertainties are included herein.     
154EU cL J         From 1988Ka01. Any conflict with those in Adopted            
154EU2cL      Levels is noted.                                                  
154EU cL T         From 1988Ka01 and for in-beam studies only. See {+154}Eu     
154EU2cL      Adopted Levels for values from all of the available data.         
