154EU c  Experimental methods:                                                  
154EU c  1975Ca22:  Produced by (p,n) on enriched (99.996%) {+154}Sm with       
154EU2c      E(p)=11 MeV. Measured |g singles and |g|g coincidences with        
154EU3c      Ge detectors.                                                      
154EU c  1976Ch08:  Produced by (p,n) on enriched (99.996%) {+154}Sm with       
154EU2c      E(p)=12.5 MeV followed by chemical separation. Measured |g's       
154EU3c      with Ge detectors and ce in magnetic spectrometer.                 
154EU c  1976Zo01:  Produced by (p,n), (d,2n), (d,|a), and (d,p); some          
154EU2c      followed by chemical separations. Measured |g singles and |g|g     
154EU3c      coincidences with Ge detectors. Si(Li) detector used in search     
154EU4c      for the isomeric transition.                                       
154EU cG           The |g transition which deexcites the isomeric level has     
154EU2cG     not been observed; and two other unobserved |g transitions are     
154EU3cG     proposed to provide feeding of the 127 and 129 levels.             
154EU cG E         From 1976Zo01. These values have the smallest                
154EU2cG      uncertainties, so a weighted average of these values with those   
154EU3cG      of 1975Ca22 and 1976Ch08 would give essentially the same values.  
154EU4cG      For most |g's, more precise energies are given in the Adopted     
154EU5cG      |g Radiations.                                                    
154EU cG RI        From 1976Ch08, unless otherwise noted. The evaluator has     
154EU2cG      increased the uncertainties by factors of 2.0 above 30 keV and    
154EU3cG      4.0 below 30 keV to allow for the large discrepancy between       
154EU4cG      the values from 1975Ca22, 1976Ch08, and 1976Zo01. The             
154EU5cG      discrepancies among the reported data are illustrated by the      
154EU6cG      fact that, for the three |g's below 34 keV, the reported          
154EU7cG      uncertainties are about 10%, but the values vary by factors       
154EU8cG      of 2 or more.                                                     
154EU cG M,MR      Assignments and values are from Adopted |g Radiations.       
154EU cL           Although the observed |g rays are similar, the decay         
154EU2cL     schemes of 1975Ca22, 1976Ch08, and 1976Zo01 are quite different.   
154EU3cL     The scheme adopted here is that of the evaluator and is based      
154EU4cL     on the level structure from the {+153}Eu(n,|g) study of 1987Ba52.  
154EU5cL     The scheme adopted in previous ENSDF evaluations                   
154EU6cL     (1979Ha02 and 1987He20) was similar to that of 1976Zo01, which     
154EU7cL     relied on certain data from the (n,|g) study of 1977St14. This     
154EU8cL     study differs in important ways from that of 1987Ba52.             
154EU cL E         Computed from these |g energies, unless otherwise noted;     
154EU2cL      for more precise values, see the Adopted Levels.                  
