154GD cG $Unplaced |g's are not included here; see {+154}Tb |e decays (21.5 h,  
154GD2cG 9.973 h, and 22.7 h), {+154}Eu |b{+-} decay, and {+152}Sm(|a,2n|g).    
154GD cG E$Where the |g is seen in both the {+154}Eu |b{+-} decay and the       
154GD2cG {+153}Gd(n,|g) reaction, the E|g value is generally taken from the     
154GD3cG latter study, unless noted otherwise. In other cases, the values are   
154GD4cG from a combination of all available values. {+154}Eu is a commonly used
154GD5cG source for calibration of |g-ray detectors. A careful analysis and     
154GD6cG evaluation of the available E|g data on the prominent |g's from the Eu 
154GD7cG |b{+-} decay has been carried out by 2000He14. Where available, these  
154GD8cG data are adopted in this evaluation.                                   
154GD cG RI$Where the |g is seen in the {+154}Eu decay, the I|g values are      
154GD2cG generally taken from those data. In other cases, they are from the     
154GD3cG combination of all available values. The uncertainties in those from   
154GD4cG the {+153}Gd(n,|g) study include only the statistical component.       
154GD5cG Significant differences between values from the various reactions and  
154GD6cG decays are noted.                                                      
154GD cG RI$For some of the I|g values from {+153}Gd(n,|g), which are marked as 
154GD2cG "multiply placed - intensity undivided", the second placement is in    
154GD3cG another isotope.                                                       
154GD cG M,MR$Values include the results from all types of experiments.         
154GD2cG Multipolarities and mixing ratios have been obtained from |g|g(|q) and 
154GD3cG |g(|q) measurements in {+152}Sm(|a,2n|g) (1978We08, 2019Ma70) and      
