154GD CL BAND(f)$K{+|p}=2+ even-spin band.                                      
154GD CL BAND(H)$K{+|p}=1- even spin band.                                      
154GD CL BAND(h)$K{+|p}=1- odd spin band.                                       
154GD CL BAND(I)$K{+|p}=4+ even-spin band.                                      
154GD2cL Dominant Configuration=(|p 3/2[411])+(|p 5/2[413]).                    
154GD2cL a=12.98, b=-0.030 (from 4+, 5+ and 6+ levels). From                    
154GD3cL single-nucleon-transfer studies, 2001Bu17 interpret this band as being 
154GD4cL a hexadecapole vibration (or a g boson excitation). 1994Wu01 (see also 
154GD5cL 1993Wu03 and 1993ApZZ), however, propose that IT is a K{+|p}=4+ |g|g   
154GD6cL vibrational band. The dominant two-quasiparticle make-up of this band  
154GD7cL argues against this latter interpretation.                             
154GD CL BAND(i)$K{+|p}=4+ odd-spin band.                                       
154GD CL BAND(Q)$Excited K{+|p}=0+ band                                         
