154GD    154EU B- DECAY                2004Ku13                  25NDS    202503
154GD  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154GD D  DATA SET COMPLETELY RE-DONE (MARCH, 2008) BY CW REICH TO INCORPORATE   
154GD2D   DATA FROM 2004Ku13, WHICH ELIMINATES SEVERAL LEVELS, A NUMBER OF      
154GD3D   PREVIOUSLY REPORTED GAMMAS, AS WELL AS BRINGING IN OTHER DATA.        
154GD c  The level scheme is primarily from 2004Ku13. This work eliminates a    
154GD2c  number of previously reported levels and sets rather stringent upper   
154GD3c  limits on the intensities of |?75 gammas that were previously          
154GD4c  associated                                                             
154GD4c  with the {+154}Gd level scheme. All the |g's listed by these authors   
154GD5c  are placed in their proposed level scheme. In earlier studies, a number
154GD6c  of |g's were shown as unplaced. In view of this recent study, the      
154GD7c  evaluator has not listed any of these previously unplaced |g's.        
154GD c  2004Ku13: measured |?2.4|*10{+8} |g-ray singles and |?1.|*10{+8} |g|g  
154GD2c  coin events using the "8|p SPECTROMETER" array of 20                   
154GD3c  Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors, having nominal active volumes of    
154GD4c  115 cm{+3}. 380 twofold coincidence combinations were available for    
154GD5c  the array. The source-detector distances were 22~cm. No absorbers were 
154GD6c  placed in front of the detectors, and only the surrounding BGO         
154GD7c  Compton-suppression detectors served to suppress the room background.  
154GD c  Data are from many measurements including |g energies from 1968Me12,   
154GD2c  1970Ri19, 1980Sh15, 1989Ki10, 1990He05, 1990Me15, and 1992Sm02; |g     
154GD3c  intensities from 1968Me12, 1969Va09, 1970Ri19, 1980Ro22, 1980Sh15,     
154GD4c  1984Iw03, 1989Ki10, 1990He05, 1990Me15, 1991BaZS, 1992Ha02, 1992Sa04,  
154GD5c  and 1992Sm02; half-lives from 1955Su64, 1961St04, 1963Bu03, 1968Ku03,  
154GD6c  1972Aw04, 1995Ma03; |b{+-} intensities from 1966Ha36 and 1968Ng01; and 
154GD7c  |g|g coincidences from 1968Me12 and 1977Gu10.  Measurements related to 
154GD8c  J{+|p}'s and |g multipolarity assignments are listed in {+154}Gd       
154GD9c  Adopted Levels and |g radiations. Other references on E|g, I|g, |g     
154GDac  multipolarities, and the decay scheme include 1959Ha07, 1960De16,      
154GDbc  1966Dz15, 1968Br20, 1968Me18, 1968Ng01, 1969An01, 1969Au09, 1969GuZW,  
154GDcc  1969Ri03, 1970Ke13, 1970Ra37, 1970Re08, 1972De12, 1972Ha84, 1974HeYW,  
154GDdc  1980Yo06, 1982Co05, 1982HoZF, 1991ZaZZ, 1992Ak03 and 2002El07; on      
154GDec  half-lives 1961Na06; and on miscellaneous properties 1960Ma38,         
154GDfc  1962Lu03, 1966Di02, 1967Ho06, 1970Wa26, 1977Ra08.  brief descriptions  
154GDgc  of the experimental methods employed in these are not given here. They 
154GDhc  are available on-line in the ENSDF file (at www.nndc.bnl.gov).         
154GD d          Evaluated x-ray emission probabilities from 2004BeZQ           
154GD d                        (in photons/100 decays)                          
154GD d                        ------------------------                         
154GD d                           L| x ray:      7.1|+0.3                       
154GD d                          K|a{-1}| x ray:     7.2|+0.2                   
154GD d                          K|a{-2}| x ray:    13.0|+0.3                   
154GD d                          K|b{-1}'| x ray:    4.1|+0.1                   
154GD d                          K|b{-2}'| x ray:    1.08|+0.3                  
154GD D  Experimental methods:                                                  
154GD D  Measurements of decay scheme including G energies and intensities:     
154GD D  1959Ha07:  Measured EG and RI for 2 G's on curved-crystal spectrometer.
154GD D  1960De16:  See notes below. Measured EG and RI for 7 G's.              
154GD D  1966Dz15:  154EU from n capture in enriched (98.9%) 153EU. G's         
154GD2D       measured from recoil electrons in magnetic spectrometer.          
154GD3D       EG and RI for 32 G's.                                             
154GD D  1968Br20:  154EU from n capture in enriched 153EU. Measured RI and I   
154GD2D       in magnetic spectrometer by internal and external conversion.     
154GD D  1968Ha28:  CE measured in magnetic spectrometer. Deduced EKC for 4 G's.
154GD D  1968Me12:  154EU from n capture in enriched 153EU and 154EU enriched   
154GD2D       after production. Ge(Li) detectors used to measure EG, RI, and    
154GD3D       GG coincidences. Give 140 RI values and 66 or 140 EG values.      
154GD D  1968Me18:  154EU from n capture in enriched 153EU and 154EU enriched   
154GD2D       after production. G measured but only results are level           
154GD3D       energies.                                                         
154GD D  1968Ng01:  154EU from n capture in enriched (98.8%) 153EU. Ge(Li)      
154GD2D       detector used to measure EG and RI for 30 G's. Measured beta      
154GD3D       on magnetic spectrometer and deduced 6 I(B-) values. Measured     
154GD4D       CE on magnetic spectrometer for 13 G's; deduced 10 EKC.           
154GD D  1969An01:  154EU from n capture in enriched (98.7%) 153EU. Measured    
154GD2D       CE in THE magnetic spectrometer (R= 0.1%). I(e-) for 8 lines.     
154GD D  1969Au09:  154EU from n capture in 153EU. Measured G's with Ge(Li)     
154GD2D        detectors. EG and RI for 13 G's.                                 
154GD D  1969GuZW:  Measured EG and RI for 23 G's.                              
154GD D  1969Ri03:  154EU from n capture in enriched 153EU. G's measured with   
154GD2D       Ge(Li) detectors and obtained 13 EG and RI.                       
154GD D  1969Va09:  Ge(Li) detector used to measure EG and RI for 48 G's.       
154GD2D       GG(THETA) measured and deduced MR for 8 G's.                      
154GD D  1970Ke13:  154EU from thermal n capture. Measured 12 EG and RI.        
154GD D  1970Ra37:  154EU from n capture in enriched (98.8%) 153EU. EG measured 
154GD2D       on curved-crystal spectrometer for 16 G's.                        
154GD D  1970Re08:  154EU from n capture. Measured 2 EG and RI with             
154GD2D       curved-crystal spectrometer.                                      
154GD D  1970Ri19:  Ge(Li) and NaI detectors used to measure EG, RI, and GG     
154GD2D       coincidences for 51 G's.                                          
154GD D  1970Ru09:  154EU from isotope separation following n capture in        
154GD2D       enriched 153EU. Used Ge(Li), NaI, and magnetic spectrometer       
154GD2D       to measure G singles, GG(THETA), GG(THETA,t), and GCE(THETA).     
154GD3D       Gives some RI and 5 MR values.                                    
154GD D  1971Ru05:  154EU from isotope separation following n capture in        
154GD2D       enriched 153EU. Measured G in Ge(Li) detector, GG(THETA) with     
154GD3D       Ge(Li) and NaI detectors, and CE in magnetic spectrometer.        
154GD4D       Gives 1 MR, 3 RI, 13 EKC, and 3 I(E0,K)/I(E2,K) ratios.           
154GD D  1972Ha84:  Review paper, quoted results from others.                   
154GD D  1972Na21:  154EU purchased. Ge(Li) detector used to measure RI for     
154GD2D       12 G's. CE measured on Si(Li) detector and deduced 20 EKC.        
154GD D  1974HeYW:  Ge(Li) detector used to measure EG and RI for 25 G's.       
154GD D  1977YoZo:  Measured RI and deduced relative B(E2) values, but no RI    
154GD2D       given. Abstract. See 1980Yo06.                                    
154GD D  1980Sh15:  154EU purchased. Ge(Li) detector for G measurements.        
154GD2D       EG and RI for 82 G's, SIGMA AP 0.3 keV and 2%, resp.              
154GD D  1980Yo06:  Ge(Li) detector used to measure RI for 26 G's above 400     
154GD2D       keV, with SIGMA AP 0.3 keV.                                       
154GD D  1982Co05:  154EU both purchased and from isotope separator group.      
154GD2D       Ge and Ge(Li) detectors used to measure RI of 8 G's with SIGMA    
154GD3D       of 0.6-1.0%.                                                      
154GD D  1982HoZF:  Measured G-emission probabilities for 9 G's.                
154GD D  1984Iw03:  Ge(Li) detector used to measure RI for G's below 450 keV.   
154GD2D       G intensities normalized by requiring 100% feeding of ground      
154GD3D       state and including results from 1980Yo06.                        
154GD D  1989Ki10: Measured G singles, GG coincidences, and GG(THETA) with Ge   
154GD2D       and NaI(Tl) detectors including Compton suppression.  Report      
154GD3D       81 EG, RI values and 10 MR values.                                
154GD D  1990He05: Measured 35 EG values and 24 RI's.                           
154GD D  1990Me15: Report 33 EG and RI values, partly related to 1968Me12.      
154GD D  1991BaZS: Evalution of RI for 12 best lines for ^IAEA-CRP of 1992;     
154GD2D       does not include 1990Me15, 1992Ha02, or 1992Sm02.                 
154GD D  1991ZaZZ: Abstract gives 13 RI values.                                 
154GD D  1992El11: MEASURED G SINGLES AND GG COINCIDENCES USING COMMERCIALLY    
154GD2D       AVAILABLE SOURCES. DISCOVERED ONE NEW G, MEASURED RI VALUES       
154GD3D       FOR SEVERAL GAMMAS FOR WHICH SUCH VALUES WERE NOT PREVIOUSLY      
154GD4D       GIVEN AND PLACED SEVERAL PREVIOUSLY OBSERVED, BUT UNPLACED, G'S.  
154GD D  1992Ha02: Measured G singles. Report 130 measured RI's and give        
154GD2D       weighted average for values from 13 references including          
154GD3D       1968Me12, 1990Me15 and 1992Sm02.                                  
154GD D  1992Sm02: Measured EG and RI for 27 G's.                               
154GD D  1997Ka47: DID NEUTRON ACTIVATION OF A 24-ELEMENT STANDARD IN SIX       
154GD2D       DIFFERENT IRRADIATION POSITIONS IN TWO DIFFERENT NUCLEAR          
154GD3D       REACTORS. USING A GENERALIZED LEAST-SQUARES ANALYSIS PROCEDURE,   
154GD4D       THESE AUTHORS WERE ABLE TO DEDUCE THERMAL-NEUTRON CROSS           
154GD5D       SECTIONS, RESONANCE INTEGRALS AND |g-EMISSION PROBABILITIES FOR   
154GD6D       THE VARIOUS NUCLIDES. FOR 154EU, THEY REPORT EMISSION-PROBABILITY 
154GD7D       VALUES FOR THE 247.9 AND 996.2 GAMMAS.                            
154GD D  2002El07: 154EU B- DECAY. MEASURED EG, RI, GG COIN USING TWO HPGe      
154GD2D       DETECTORS AND A Compton-suppression SYSTEM CONSISTING OF A HPGe   
154GD3D       DETECTOR SURROUNDED BY A 9"|*9" ANNULAR NaI(Tl) SINGLE CRYSTAL.   
154GD4D       REPORT RELATIVE RI VALUES AND LEVEL SCHEME.                       
154GD D  Measurements of multipolarities:                                       
154GD D  1960De16:  154EU from n capture in enriched (95%) 153EU. GG(THETA)     
154GD2D       measured with NaI detectors.  Deduced MR for 5 G's.               
154GD D  1961Ba19:                                                              
154GD D  1964Ca12:  Measured circular polarization of 1274 G and deduced MR for 
154GD2D       G and J of 1397 level.                                            
154GD D  1964Ha47:  Measured CE with magnetic spectrometer, G with NaI detector,
154GD2D       and GCE coincidences. Deduced MR for 3 G's and EKC for 5 G's.     
154GD D  1966Dz15:  See comments above. Deduced 8 or 11 MR.                     
154GD D  1969Ha01:  GG(THETA) measured with Ge(Li) and NaI detectors. Deduced   
