154GD D  1969Ha36:  GG(THETA) measured with Ge(Li) and NaI detectors. Deduced   
154GD2D       MR for 6 G's.                                                     
154GD D  1969Va09:  See comments above. Deduced 8 MR.                           
154GD D  1971La11:  GG(THETA) and GG(THETA,t) measured with Ge and NaI detectors
154GD2D       Deduced MR for 2 G's.                                             
154GD D  1971Ma65:  GCE(THETA) and GG(THETA) measured. CE measured in magnetic  
154GD2D       spectrometer. Deduced MR and EKC for 1 G.                         
154GD D  1971Wh01:  154EU from n capture in enriched 153EU. GG(THETA) measured  
154GD2D       with Ge(Li) and NaI detectors. Deduce MR for 5 G's and            
154GD3D       associated level spins.                                           
154GD D  1972De12:  Description of GG(THETA) measurement system.                
154GD D  1972Go35:  154EU from n capture in enriched 153EU. GG(THETA) measured  
154GD2D       with Ge(Li) detectors. Deduced MR for 7 G's and level spins.      
154GD D  1973Ob01:  GG(THETA) measured with Ge(Li) and NaI detectors. Deduced   
154GD2D       MR for 4 G's.                                                     
154GD D  1974Lo02:  Comments on expected E1,M2 mixtures. No new data.           
154GD D  1977Gu10:  Ge(Li) and NaI detectors used to measure G singles and      
154GD2D       GG and GG(THETA) coincidences. Deduced MR for 19 G's. EG and RI   
154GD3D       given for AP 75 G's.                                              
154GD D  1983Gi07:  154EU from n capture in enriched (AP 98%) 153EU.            
154GD2D       Measured GG(THETA), GCE(THETA), and G(THETA) from oriented        
154GD3D       nuclei. Deduced MR for 15 G's.                                    
154GD D  1983Le19:  GG(THETA) and GGG(THETA) measured with Ge(Li) and NaI       
154GD2D       detectors. Deduced MR for 1 G.                                    
154GD D  1992Ak03:  MEASURED GG(THETA) AND CEK-G(THETA). REPORTED MR VALUES FOR 
154GD2D       9 G TRANSITIONS.                                                  
154GD D  1996Al31:  MEASURED GG(THETA) USING THE 12 ^Ge DETECTORS FROM THE      
154GD2D       ^OSIRIS FACILITY, THE DETECTORS BEING MOUNTED IN A RING AROUND    
154GD3D        THE SOURCE. THESE AUTHORS MEASURED MR FOR THE 3+|)2+ TRANSITION  
154GD4D        WITHIN THE GAMMA BAND. FROM THIS, AND THE PREVIOUSLY KNOWN       
154GD5D        G-FACTOR OF THE 2+ MEMBER OF THE GS BAND, THEY DETERMINED THE    
154GD6D        G-FACTOR OF THE 2+ MEMBER OF THE GAMMA BAND.                     
154GD D  Measurements of lifetimes:                                             
154GD D  1961Na06:  No source data. GG coincidences for 2+ lifetime.            
154GD D  1961St04:  154EU from n capture in enriched 153EU. Measured lifetime   
154GD2D       of 2+ state in course of GG(THETA,H) study.                       
154GD D  1963Bu03:  154EU from n capture in enriched (97%) target. Measured     
154GD2D       lifetimes of first 2+ and 4+ states by B-CE coincidences in       
154GD3D       double-lens spectrometer.                                         
154GD D  1968Ku03:  154EU source. Measured lifetime of 2+ state from B-CE       
154GD2D       coincidences with two plastic scintillators.                      
154GD D  1972Aw04:  154EU from n capture. Measured lifetimes of first 2+ and 4+ 
154GD2D       states with two magnetic lens CE spectrometers.                   
154GD D  1978Ag03:  Calculated B(E2) from model. Tallies measurements.          
154GD D  1995Ma03:  MEASURED T OF THE FIRST 2+ STATE USING A "FAST-TIMING"      
154GD2D   BGG(t) METHOD. ALSO DEDUCED AN ICC VALUE FOR THE 2+ TO 0+ TRANSITION  
154GD3D   USING THIS T VALUE AND A "BEST" BE2 VALUE FROM OTHER SOURCES.         
154GD D  Measurements of B- shapes and other B- decay related properties:       
154GD D       These measurements generally do not give data for any data sets.  
154GD D  1960La04:  Measured B- shape and deduced shape factor and E(B-).       
154GD D  1961Sa10:  Measured B(1860)G(123)(THETA) and deduced B matrix elements.
154GD D  1961Su08:  Measured BG(THETA) and deduced B matrix elements.           
154GD D  1961Wy04:  Measured BG(THETA) and deduced B matrix elements.           
154GD D  1962Bh02:  Measured BG(THETA) and deduced B matrix elements.           
154GD D  1963He09:  Measured BG circular polarization, deduced on JPI.          
154GD D  1963Su08:  Measured BG(THETA) and change of correlation with E(B-).    
154GD D  1964Du03:  Recalculated B matrix elements.                             
154GD D  1964Li05:  Reanalyzed B matrix elements.                               
154GD D  1966Ci02:  Measured BG(THETA).                                         
154GD D  1966Ha36:  Measured BG coincidences to deduced E(B-) and IB for two    
154GD2D        branches.                                                        
154GD D  1968Zg01:  Measured BG(THETA) and change of correlation with E(B-).    
154GD D  1969Su09:  Measured BG(THETA).                                         
154GD D  1977Ra08:  Measured B- shape factor. Deduced E(B-) and matrix elements 
154GD D  1978RaYT:  Measured BGG(THETA).                                        
154GD D  Other measurements:                                                    
154GD D  1960Ma38:  Measured GG(THETA,H,t) to deduce g factor of 2+ state.      
154GD D  1961Ba19:  Measured GG polarization (THETA) to deduced JPI of 1 level. 
154GD D  1961St04:  Measured GG(THETA,H,t) to deduce g factor of 2+ state.      
154GD D  1962Lu03:  154EU from n capture. Measure GG coincidence rates with     
154GD2D       NaI detectors. Deduced ICC and EKC for 1 G.                       
154GD D  1964Ca12:  154EU from n capture in enriched (99%) 153EU. BG(THETA)     
154GD2D       to determine circular polarization. Deduced 1 J value.            
154GD D  1966Di02:  154EU from n capture. Measure GG coincidence rates with     
154GD2D       NaI detectors. Deduced ICC and EKC for 1 G. Same results as       
154GD3D       1962Lu03.                                                         
154GD D  1966Ha36:  154EU from n capture in enriched (99.0%) 153EU. Beta shapes 
154GD2D       measured in magnetic spectrometer in coincidence with G.          
154GD D  1967Ho06:  154EU from n capture in enriched 153EU. GCE(THETA) measured 
154GD2D       with magnetic spectrometer and NaI detector. GG(THETA) measured   
154GD3D       with NaI detectors. Deduced particle parameters for 2 G's.        
154GD D  1970Wa26:  154EU from thermal n capture. GG(THETA,H,t) measured        
154GD2D       to obtain g factor of 2+ state.                                   
154GD D  1977Ra08:  154EU from n capture in enriched (99%) 153EU. B- shape      
154GD2D       in coincidence with 123 G measured with magnetic spectrometer.    
154GD cB $Beta-spectral shape factors are given by 1960La04, 1966Ha36, 1968Ng01,
154GD2cB and 1977Ra08. |b|g(|q) has been measured by 1961Sa10, 1961Su08,        
154GD3cB 1961Wy04, 1962Bh02, 1963Su08, 1966Ci02, 1968Zg01, 1969Su09, and        
154GD4cB 1978RaYT. |b|g circular polarization has been measured by 1963He09.    
154GD5cB |b{+-} decay matrix elements have been computed in many of these       
154GD6cB papers, as well as in 1964Du03 and 1964Li05.                           
154GD cB IB$Average of measured values from 1966Ha36 and 1968Ng01, unless noted 
154GD2cB as from |g-transition intensity balances. Where the measured values are
154GD3cB given, the intensity-balance values are also given as as comments and  
154GD4cB are in excellent agreement. The total |b{+-} intensity listed is       
154GD5cB 100.4%. The following levels (and upper limits on the intensities of   
154GD6cB the feeding |b{+-} transitions) are not observed by 2004Ku13: 1135.96  
154GD7cB (<0.0073); 1233 (<0.0049); 1276.63 (<0.0039); 1293.59 (<0.0051);       
154GD8cB 1294.17 (<0.0083); 1295.467 (<0.0091); 1510.1 (<0.0086); 1698.2        
154GD9cB (<0.0006); 1770.5 (<0.0045); 1838.3 (<0.0023); 1861.2 (<0.0008); 1879.0
154GDacB (<0.0003); and 1894.7 (<0.0017). Note that these limits are given      
154GDbcB relative to I|g(1274|g)=100. To express them in transitions per 100    
154GDccB decays, multiply by 0.3484.                                            
154GD cB E(R)$From 1966Ha36.                                                    
154GD cB E(S)$From 1968Ng01.                                                    
154GD cB IB(T)$From |g-transition intensity balance.                            
154GD cG $The indicated placements of the |g's in the level scheme are supported
154GD2cG by the |g|g-coincidence relations from 2004Ku13, as well as from       
154GD3cG 1968Me12 and 1977Gu10. These are not specifically shown on the         
154GD4cG level-scheme drawing.                                                  
154GD cG RI$The I|g values for the prominent |g rays are important because      
154GD2cG {+154}Eu is used as an efficiency calibration standard for Ge          
154GD3cG detectors.  For this reason, some of these I|g values were given       
154GD4cG detailed consideration by the Decay Data Evaluation Project, a program 
154GD5cG carried out under the auspices of the IAEA. The {+154}Eu data were     
154GD6cG evaluated by V.P. Chechev and N.K. Kuzmenko and included all the data  
154GD7cG available to them. Their results are given in 2004BeZQ. The data       
154GD8cG reported by 2004Ku13 were not included in their work, but are in       
154GD9cG generally good agreement with it.                                      
154GD cG RI$Values of the absolute emission probabilities of the {+154}Eu-decay 
154GD2cG |g's have also recently been measured by 2004Te01. These values are in 
154GD3cG generally in good agreement with the evaluated values of Chechev and   
154GD4cG Kuzmenko, as well as with those of 2004Ku13.                           
154GD cG E$Values are from 2004Ku13, unless noted otherwise.                    
154GD cG E(P)$From the recommended values in the analysis and evaluation of     
154GD2cG 2000He14.                                                              
154GD cG RI$Relative values, from 2004Ku13 unless noted otherwise.              
154GD cG M,MR$Assignments and values are from {+154}Gd adopted |g radiations and
154GD2cG include the results of all types of experiments and all decay modes.   
154GD3cG See {+154}Gd adopted |g radiations for other information including: (1)
154GD4cG mixing ratios such as |d(M3/E2) and |d(M2/E1) where |d can be zero and 
154GD5cG is not included here; (2) comments on measurements for lines which are 
154GD6cG multiplets; and (3) identification of |a values that are based on      
154GD7cG experimental values rather than theory.                                
154GD cL E$From a least-squares fit to the |g-ray energies. Three E|g's out of  
154GD2cL 135 differ by more than 3|s.                                           
154GD cL J$From Adopted Levels.                                                 
154GD cL T$Adopted values.                                                      
