154GD    154TB EC DECAY (21.5 H)       1975SO03,1972VY04         25NDS    202503
154GD  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154GD D  DATA SET UPGRADED (APRIL, 2008) BY CW REICH TO INCORPORATE A NEW  Q    
154GD2D   VALUE FOR THE PARENT RECORD, ADD CC VALUES FROM BRICC, AND TO MODIFY  
154GD3D   A NUMBER OF COMMENTS.                                                 
154GD c  2013Be38 and 2014BeZX compiled for the XUNDL database by               
154GD2c  M. S. Basunia (LBNL)                                                   
154GD c  Three {+154}Tb isomers (21.5, 9.4, and 22.7 h) have been observed. The 
154GD2c  most complete decomposition of the |g data among these isomers is from 
154GD3c  1975So03, so these data are used to place the |g's.                    
154GD c  A study of the {+154}Tb isomers is reported as a part of the thesis    
154GD2c  which constitutes 2001KuZS. These data are not included here, since    
154GD3c  further analysis appears to be required.                               
154GD D  Experimental methods:                                                  
154GD D  1961Ha23: Measured CE in magnetic spectrographs. Report 30 G's from    
154GD2D       9-H decay and 47 G's from 22-H decay.                             
154GD D  1969Ba16: 154TB from 151EU(A,N) reaction on enriched target. Measured  
154GD2D       G singles and GG coincidences with NaI(Tl) and Ge detectors.      
154GD3D       Report energies for about 22 G's and GG coincidences.             
154GD D  1969Cl11: Report energies for 41 G's.                                  
154GD D  1970Ag02: 154TB from 154GD(d,2n) reaction on enriched (66%) target at  
154GD2D       13.6 MeV. Measured B+ in B+ G coincidence system.  Report         
154GD3D       E(B+) and I(B+) for branches to two 0+ states.                    
154GD D  1971Ri08: 154TB from 153EU(A,3n) reaction at 36 MeV and 155GD(p,2n)    
154GD2D       reaction at 15 MeV. Measured G singles and GG coincidences and    
154GD3D       saw 300 G's, but no EG or RI reported. Shows partial decay scheme 
154GD4D       of I=7 isomer. See 1975So03 for report of all data.               
154GD d  1972Vy04: {+154}Tb from spallation reaction on Ta target with 680-MeV  
154GD2d  p. Measured T{-1/2} of two isomers.                                    
154GD D  1973Ba20: 154TB from spallation reaction on Ta target with 680-MeV p.  
154GD2D       Measured IT branching intensities.                                
154GD D  1973La20: 154TB from (p,xn) reaction on natural Gd. Measured T of      
154GD2D       the three isomers and the IT branching intensities.               
154GD D  1975Gr44: Summary of lab work, see 1972Vy04.                           
154GD c  1975So03: {+154}Tb from {+153}Eu(|a,3n) reaction on enriched (99%)     
154GD2c  target at 36 MeV, same reaction on natural Eu target at 38 MeV with    
154GD3c  chemical and isotope separations, and {+155}Gd(p,2n) reaction on       
154GD4c  enriched (91.8%) target at 15 MeV. Measured |g singles and |g|g        
154GD5c  coincidences with Ge detectors. Report 159 |g's from 9.4-h decay,      
154GD6c  155 |g's from 21.5-h decay, and 51 |g's from 22.7-h decay.             
154GD D  1977Ya04: 154TB from 155GD(p,2n), 156GD(p,3n), and 153EU(A,3n)         
154GD2D       reactions. Measured G singles and GG coincidence with Ge          
154GD3D       detectors and CE in magnetic spectrometer. CE data for 22 G's.    
154GD4D       Scheme give without relationship to a specific isomer of Tb.      
154GD D  1978We08: Measured GG(THETA) to deduce G multipolarity and JPI.        
154GD D  1980By03: Report B-feeding distribution from total-absorption G        
154GD2D       spectrometer. No parent half-life is given.                       
154GD D  1981Fe01: 154TB from spallation of Ta target with 660 MeV p. G(THETA)  
154GD2D       measured from nuclei oriented in Gd matrix in external magnetic   
154GD3D       field. Report about 34 MR values.                                 
154GD c  2013Be38, 2014BeZX: {+154}Tb isomer populated by {+154}Gd(p,n)         
154GD2c  reaction with E{-p}=12 MeV at Tandem accelerator of University of      
154GD2c  Cologne. Measured off beam |g and |g|g spectra                         
154GD3c  with 14 HPGe detectors and reported |g-ray branching ratios for five   
154GD4c  levels. Deduced reduced transition strengths                           
154GD5c  combining data of resonant photon-scattering cross sections            
154GD6c  for {+154}Gd(|g,|g') reaction (see dataset). Theory:                   
154GD7c  Calculated Nuclear Matrix Elements (NME) for neutrinoless double beta  
154GD7c  decay. Interacting Boson Model (IBM-2) and Energy Density Functional   
154GD8c  (EDF) model calculations.                                              
154GD c  Others: 1961Ha23, 1969Ba16, 1969Cl11, 1970Ag02, 1971Ri08, 1973Ba20,    
154GD2c  1973La20, 1975Gr44, 1977Ya04, 1978We08, 1980By03, 1981Fe01             
154GD c  The 2009Re14 evaluation presents a normalization of this level         
154GD2c  scheme deduced based on the |g-ray intensity balance and the ratio     
154GD2c  I|b{++}(681)/I|b{++}(g.s.)=0.31 measured by 1970Ag02, as well as       
154GD2c  the log| {Ift} > 8.5 limits for both these branches.                   
154GD2c  However, without a more secure determination of I(|e+|b{++})(g.s.),    
154GD2c  this gives only a plausible version of the |e+|b{++} decay scheme.     
154GD2c  In order to prompt remeasuring this decay scheme, this evaluation      
154GD2c  does no longer present the |e+|b{++} data.                             
154GD c  1970Ag02 measured end point energies of 2450 {I50} and 1860 {I50}      
154GD2c  for beta decays to g.s. and 671 levels, respectively.                  
