154GD  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154GD D  DATA SET UPGRADED (MAY, 2008) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE BAND ASSIGNMENTS, 
154GD2D  DCO RATIOS, CONFIGURATION ASSIGNMENTS AND NUMEROUS COMMENTS.           
154GD c  {+150}Nd({+9}Be,5n|g), E({+9}Be)=55 MeV; measured E|g, I|g,            
154GD2c  and |g|g(|q) in the TESSA2 multidetector array, consisting of          
154GD3c  six escape-suppressed Ge detectors and a 50-element BGO crystal        
154GD4c  ball. Report level scheme and an interpretation in terms of a          
154GD5c  cranked shell-model calculation.                                       
154GD t          Band-labeling convention for neutrons                          
154GD t            ---------------------------------                            
154GD t                A     (|a=+1/2, |p=+){-1}                                
154GD t                B     (|a=-1/2, |p=+){-1}                                
154GD t                C     (|a=+1/2, |p=+){-2}                                
154GD t                D     (|a=-1/2. |p=+){-2}                                
154GD t                E     (|a=+1/2, |p=-){-1}                                
154GD t                F     (|a=-1/2, |p=-){-1}                                
154GD t                X     (|a=+1/2, |p=-)                                    
154GD t                Y     (|a=-1/2, |p=-)                                    
154GD t            ---------------------------------                            
154GD t          At ~h|w=0, the labels X and Y correspond                       
154GD t          to the 11/2-[505] Nilsson orbital,                             
154GD t          A and B to 3/2+[651] Nilsson orbital, and                      
154GD t          C and D to 1/2+[660] Nilsson orbital.                          
154GD cG RI$Relative values, normalized to I|g(248.0|g)=100, at                 
154GD2cG E({+9}Be)=55~MeV.                                                      
154GD cG M$Values are based on the measured DCO-ratio data. 1989Mo20 point out  
154GD2cG that DCO ratios near 1.0 correspond to stretched quadrupoles, while    
154GD3cG those near 0.6 correspond to stretched dipoles. Pure dipoles with      
154GD4cG |DJ=0 are distinguished from stretched quadrupoles on the basis of the 
154GD5cG implications for the J{+|p} values of nearby states. These             
154GD6cG multipolarities are not included in the Adopted Gammas data set.       
154GD cL J         Authors' assignments, which are based on deduced |g          
154GD2cL  multipolarities and band structure, as well as the previously known   
154GD3cL  assignments. These are in agreement with the Adopted Values, unless   
154GD4cL  noted otherwise.                                                      
154GD CL BAND(A)$K{+|p}=0+ ground-state band.                                   
154GD CL BAND(B)$First excited K{+|p}=0+ band. Probable |b{+-}vibration.        
154GD CL BAND(C)$Aligned two-neutron-quasiparticle band.                        
154GD2cL Configuration=AB                                                       
154GD2cL crosses the g.s. band at ~h|w=0.31~MeV (near the 18+ level).           
154GD CL BAND(D)$K{+|p}=0- octupole-vibrational band. At higher spins, it can be
154GD2cL ascribed to the cranked shell-model configuration AE.                  
154GD CL BAND(E)$Band interpreted as the two-neutron-quasiparticle configuration
154GD2cL AF. Crossed by the configuration |bc near ~h|w=0.30~MeV, with          
154GD3cL configuration becoming AFBC.                                           
154GD CL BAND(F)$Band interpreted as the two-neutron-quasiparticle configuration
154GD2cL Ay                                                                     
154GD CL BAND(H)$Band interpreted as the two-neutron-quasiparticle configuration
154GD2cL AX                                                                     
154GD CL BAND(I)$Level sequence                                                 
154GD PN                                                                     5  
154GD  L    0         0+                                                    A   
154GD  L  123.1    1  2+                                                    A   
154GD  G  123.1    1  100       (E2)                                            
154GD cG $DCO=0.90~{I2}                                                         
