154GD    152SM(A,2NG),154SM(A,4NG)                               25NDS    202503
154GD  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154GD D  UPDATED (MAY, 2008) BY CW REICH TO RELABEL BAND ASSIGNMENT FOR LEVELS  
154GD2D   NOW ASSIGNED TO THE ALIGNED TWO-QUASINEUTRON BAND, THE REASSIGNMENT   
154GD3D   OF THE 842.6 GAMMA, AND INTERCHANGING THE BAND ASSIGNMENTS OF THE     
154GD4c  18+ levels at 4016 and 4087 keV.                                       
154GD c  2019Ma70 was compiled for the XUNDL database by E.A. McCutchan         
154GD2c  (NNDC, BNL)                                                            
154GD c  2011Sh07 was compiled for the XUNDL database by B. Singh (McMaster)    
154GD c  Data are from: {+152}Sm(|a,2n|g), E(|a)=24 MeV (1978We08 and           
154GD2c       1973Kh07) and E(|a)=26 MeV (1994Wu01 and 1993Wu03) and            
154GD3c       {+154}Sm(|a,4n|g), E(|a) |? 40 MeV (1973Wa33).                    
154GD4c       Others: {+152}Sm(|a,2n|g) -1966Lo11, 1968Ej01, 1972Re04, and      
154GD5c       1982Da12; {+154}Sm(|a,4n|g) -1965Ej01, 1971Fe04, 1972Fe08,        
154GD6c       1973Wa12, 1973Wa33, and 1974Go30.                                 
154GD c  The level scheme is that of 1978We08, except where                     
154GD2c       noted otherwise.                                                  
154GD c  Experimental methods:                                                  
154GD c  1965Ej01: (|a,4n|g) with E=40 MeV; measured anisotropy of ce for       
154GD2c       5 |g's up 10+ level.                                              
154GD c  1966Lo11: (|a,2n|g), E(|a)=18-20.5 MeV; measured ce in magnetic        
154GD2c       spectrometer including ce-|g coincidences. Report ce for 37       
154GD3c       |g's and levels to 10+ in two bands.                              
154GD c  1968Ej01: (|a,2n|g) and (|a,4n|g), E(|a)=36 and 40 MeV; measured       
154GD2c       ce in magnetic spectrometer; Report 8 |g's and levels to          
154GD3c       12+ in ground-state band.                                         
154GD c  1968Wi16: (|a,4n|g), E=40.5 MeV.                                       
154GD c  1969FeZZ: Abstract, see 1972Fe08.                                      
154GD c  1971Fe04: (|a,4n|g), E(|a)=42 MeV; measured |g's in Ge detector.       
154GD2c       Report a few branching ratios.                                    
154GD c  1972Fe08: (|a,4n|g), E(|a)=40 MeV. Report two new levels.              
154GD c  1972Re04: (|a,2n|g), E(|a)=27-32 MeV; measured E|g, I|g(|q),           
154GD2c       and |g|g coincidences. Report more levels.                        
154GD c  1973GoYQ: (|a,4n|g); see 1974Go30.                                     
154GD c  1973Kh07: (|a,2n|g), E(|a)=24 MeV and (|a,4n|g), E(|a)=41-50           
154GD2c       MeV; measured excitation functions, |g singles, and |g|g          
154GD3D       coincidences. Report levels to 18+ in two bands.                  
154GD c  1973Wa12: (|a,4n|g), E(|a)=38 and 41 MeV; measured excitation          
154GD2c       functions, |g(|q), and |g|g coincidences. Report levels to 16+.   
154GD c  1973Wa33: Same experimental arrangement as 1973Wa12.                   
154GD c  1974Go30: (|a,4n|g), E(|a)=45 MeV; measured ce with magnetic           
154GD2c       transport system and Si(Li) detector. Report |a{-K}(exp) and      
154GD2c       E0/E2 ratios.                                                     
154GD d  1975ZoZS: Theory                                                       
154GD c  1976WeZP: Abstract, see 1978We08.                                      
154GD c  1978We08: (|a,2n|g), E(|a)=24 MeV; measured |g(|q) at seven            
154GD2c       angles and |g|g coincidences. Report many |d values.              
154GD c  1982Da12: (|a,2n|g); measured |g linear polarization correlation.      
154GD2c       Report J|p and |d.                                                
154GD c  1993Wu03: See 1994Wu01 for measurement arrangement. Report             
154GD2c       data for 4+ band at 1646 keV.                                     
154GD c  1994Wu01: (|a,2n|g), E(|a)=26 MeV; measured |g singles, |g|g           
154GD2c       coincidences, |g(|q), and DCO ratios in an array of               
154GD2c       five 30%-efficient HPGe detectors with anti-Compton shields.      
154GD c  2011Sh07: (|a,4n|g), E=45 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g,                
154GD2c  |g|g(|q)(DCO) using AFRODITE array of eight HPGe clover detectors      
154GD3c  in Anti-Compton BGO shields. No evidence of double |b vibration        
154GD4c  below 1.5 MeV. Only partial results related to the excited 0+ band     
154GD5c  are reported in this paper. Only levels are given for the              
154GD5c  negative parity bands                                                  
154GD c  2019Ma70: (|a,2n|g), E(|a)=25 MeV from iThemba laboratory, with        
154GD2c  4 mg/cm{+2}-thick target. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |g|g(|q) and        
154GD3c  |g|g(lin pol) using the AFRODITE array.                                
154GD cG $For most of the E|g values of the {+152}Sm(|a,2n|g),{+154}Sm(|a,4n|g) 
154GD2cG dataset in the preceding 2009Re14                                      
154GD2cG evaluation no |DE|g's were listed in the original articles and         
154GD2cG therefore no |DE|g values were adopted in these situations. The newer  
154GD2cG measurement published by 2019Ma70 list a complete set of E|g,|DE|g     
154GD2cG values, however with the E|g values systematically smaller than those  
154GD2cG of 2009Re14.                                                           
154GD cG $The other newer measurement published by 2011Sh07 (done by            
154GD2cG essentially the same experimental setup and group as 2019Ma70) list    
154GD2cG rounded-to-keV E|g values, which are very close to those in the        
154GD2cG 2009Re14 evaluation, with no |DE|g values. The E|g values of 2019Ma70  
154GD2cG are also systematically smaller than the corresponding adopted |g      
154GD2cG values, which singularizes the 2019Ma70 E|g values.                    
154GD cG $In order to rescale the 2019Ma70 E|g's, the evaluator recalibrated    
154GD2cG them using a quadratic regression between two selected sets (each of   
154GD2cG 42 values) from 2019Ma70 and 2009Re14. The recalibrated E|g values are 
154GD2cG replacing the original values of 2019Ma70 in the |g table              
154GD dG $Recalibration 2nd degree polyn to get x=2019Ma70 compatible with      
154GD2dG y=2009Re14 (and 2011Sh07):                                             
154GD2dG y= -0.0000005592x^2 + 1.0023826149x - 0.0068805018                     
154GD dG $E|g's from 2019Ma70 used in the quadratic regression on x axis        
154GD2dG 122.86, 231.66, 247.44, 266.91, 303.86, 317.63, 341.96, 345.9,         
154GD2dG 377.23, 389.96, 404.76, 426.0, 427.11, 435.80, 436.89, 443.61,         
154GD2dG 462.73, 491.8, 546.64, 555.90, 591.98, 610.85, 625.87, 646.86,         
154GD2dG 664.45, 675.17, 713.18, 755.20, 813.88, 886.86, 890.97, 922.66,        
154GD2dG 983.5, 993.05, 994.32, 1002.78, 1037.23, 1047.98, 1059.31, 1090.65,    
154GD2dG 1138.56, 1233.10                                                       
154GD dG $E|g's from 2009Re14 used in the quadratic regression on y axis        
154GD2dG 123.1, 232.1, 248.0, 267.3, 304.75, 318.2, 343.0, 346.7, 378.4,        
154GD2dG 390.6, 405.6, 427.0, 427.8, 437, 437.6, 445, 463.5, 492.6, 547.5,      
154GD2dG 556.8, 592.9, 612.1, 627.2, 648.4, 665.86, 676.6, 714.75, 756.66,      
154GD2dG 815.5, 888.69, 892.62, 924.1, 984.5, 994.9, 996.36, 1004.80, 1039.2,   
154GD2dG 1050.1, 1061.38, 1092.46, 1140.54, 1235.11                             
154GD cG E$Values given are from 1978We08, unless otherwise noted. In 1978We08, 
154GD2cG some |g's do not appear in their |g data table, but do appear in their 
154GD3cG decay-scheme table.                                                    
154GD cG RI$From 1978We08 for the (|a,2n|g) reaction at 24 MeV, unless          
154GD2cG  otherwise noted. For the values from 1978We08, the evaluator has      
154GD3cG  added a 5% uncertainty, since the authors indicate there is an        
154GD4cG  additional uncertainty of |> 5%. Other (|a,2n|g) values are           
154GD5cG  given by 1972Re04 and 1968Ej01, and (|a,4n|g) values are given by     
154GD6cG  1973Wa33 and 1968Ej01. ce intensities for (|a,2n|g) are given by      
154GD7cG  1966Lo11.                                                             
154GD cG M,MR$Assignments are from adopted |g radiations and include results of 
154GD2cG all experiments. For these |a-induced reaction studies, the            
154GD3cG multipolarity and |d information are given as follows: for the         
154GD4cG {+152}Sm(|a,2n|g) reaction, by |g(|q) data (1978We08), as well as by   
154GD4cG DCO and polarization measurements (2019Ma70);                          
154GD4cG and for the {+154}Sm(|a,4n|g) reaction, by |a data (1974Go30).         
154GD cG E(V)$From 1973Kh07.                                                    
154GD cG E(Y)$From 1973Kh07 and 1973Wa33.                                       
154GD cG E(X)$From 1994Wu01 and 1993Wu03 (including |DE|g)                      
154GD cG E(W)$Spectral peak is a doublet (1978We08); E|g from level energies.   
154GD cG E(x)$From 2019Ma70 (recalibrated by evaluator as described above)      
154GD cG E(y)$Unc from 2019Ma70.                                                
154GD cG E(v)$From 2011Sh07.                                                    
154GD cL E$From a least-squares fit to the |g energies. For the                 
154GD2cL rounded-to-keV E|g's with no unc, |DE|g=1 keV was assigned             
154GD2cL for the least-squares fit                                              
154GD cL J$Adopted from the references used in this dataset based on |g-ray     
154GD2cL multipolarities                                                        
154GD cL T         From 1978We08.                                               
154GD cL E(Q)$1994Wu01 show this level on their level scheme as being populated 
154GD2cL in their (|a,2n) study, but give no supporting evidence (such as |g    
154GD3cL feeding or deexcitation) for it. The level energy is that reported by  
154GD4cL these authors. This level was not reported in the earlier |a-induced   
154GD5cL reaction studies, although it is seen in other types of experiments.   
154GD cL E(q),J(q)$2011Sh07 list E(level) and J values with no                  
154GD2cL arguments other than placement in band sequences (most of which        
154GD2cL do not have any interconnecting |g transitions)                        
154GD cL E(S)$Level proposed by 1973Kh07 and 1973Wa33.                          
154GD cL E(T)$Level proposed by 1973Kh07.                                       
154GD CL BAND(A)$K{+|p}=0+ ground-state band.                                   
154GD CL BAND(B)$First excited K{+|p}=0+ band. Probable |b-vibrational band.    
154GD CL BAND(b)$Aligned two-neutron-quasiparticle band. Cranked shell-model    
154GD2cL configuration=AB. 2011Sh07 consider this band as continuing band B     
154GD CL BAND(C)$K{+|p}=2+ |g-vibrational band.                                 
154GD CL BAND(D)$K{+|p}=1- odd-spin octupole-vibrational band.                  
154GD CL BAND(d)$K{+|p}=1- even-spin octupole-vibrational band.                 
154GD CL BAND(E)$  KPI=0+ band.                                                 
154GD2cL Excitation built on the g.s. band                                      
154GD CL BAND(F)$K{+|p}=2+ odd-spin band. 2011Sh07 do not give the 8+ member of 
154GD2cL this band                                                              
154GD CL BAND(f)$K{+|p}=2+ even-spin band.                                      
154GD CL BAND(I)$K{+|p}=4+ even-spin band.                                      
154GD2cL Dominant Configuration=(|p 3/2[411])+(|p                               
154GD2cL 5/2[413]).  From single-nucleon transfer-reaction data, 2001Bu17 have  
154GD3cL established that this band has a large component of this               
154GD4cL two-quasiproton state. They propose that this band is, consequently, a 
154GD5cL hexadecapole vibration. On the other hand, 1994Wu01 (see also 1993Wu03,
154GD6cL 1993ApZZ) propose that it is a two-phonon K{+|p}=4+ |g-vibrational     
154GD7cL band. This latter is not adopted in this evaluation.                   
154GD CL BAND(i)$K{+|p}=4+ odd-spin band.                                       
154GD CL BAND(K)$K{+|p}=7- band. Configuration=(|n 3/2[651])+(|n 11/2[505]).    
154GD CL BAND(M)$K{+|p}=7+ band. Configuration=(|n 3/2[521])+(|n 11/2[505]).    
154GD CL BAND(H)$ KPI=1- band, even spin.                                       
154GD2cL Octupole vibration built on the second vacuum band. 2011Sh07 do not    
154GD2cL give the 6- member of this band                                        
