154GD  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154GD D  DATA SET REVISED (FEBRUARY, 2008) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE MODIFICATIONS 
154GD2D   TO THE LEVEL SCHEME INDICATED BY THE LATEST 154EU B- DECAY STUDY BY   
154GD3D   2004Ku13, RECOMPUTED CC VALUES, SOME REVISED JPI VALUES AND COMMENTS. 
154GD c  Data are from the {+152}Gd(n,|g){+153}Gd(n,|g) reaction. Since 3- and  
154GD2c  4-fold capture occurs, |g's are observed in four nuclides, as well as a
154GD3c  few from isotopic and chemical impurities in the sample.               
154GD c  In a study of the |b{+-} decay of {+154}Eu and based on a combination  
154GD2c  of criteria, 2004Ku13 conclude that the following {+154}Gd levels,     
154GD2c  previously reported in (n,|g), do not exist:                           
154GD3c  1276.99; 1294.19; 1295.09; 1698.51; 1702.04; 1838.61; and 1861.55.     
154GD2c  Thus, these levels are generally decayed by very weak |g               
154GD4c  rays (below estimated detection limits), or with unknown primary |g's, 
154GD4c  or later placed elsewhere in the level scheme, or undetected by other  
154GD4c  authors, etc. These levels, as well as their deexciting |g's, are not  
154GD7c  included here. For a listing of this information see 1996SpZZ or the   
154GD8c  previous Nuclear Data Sheets evaluation (1998Re22). Elimination of     
154GD9c  these data has led to revised band assignments for some of the levels. 
154GD cG $There are many unplaced |g's, but most not are listed here because the
154GD2cG authors have not assigned any of them to particular nuclides. |a       
154GD3cG subsequent study of the {+154}Eu |b{+-} decay has shown that the       
154GD4cG placement of several |g's in the (n,|g) reaction are likely incorrect. 
154GD5cG These cases are indicated, with appropriate comments.                  
154GD cG $Several minor discrepancies exist in the |g data between different    
154GD2cG tables in this reference. In these cases, the evaluator has chosen to  
154GD3cG use the values from their |g-ray "line list" (their table 1).          
154GD cG E$Values corrected for nuclear recoil (1996SpZZ).                      
154GD cG RI$Uncertainties are the statistical component only.                   
154GD cG M$All assignments are from this reference and based on |a(K)exp data.  
154GD2cG Most of the assignments in parentheses are from doublet peaks, where   
154GD3cG the combination of the two assignments is compatible with the measured 
154GD4cG data; these assignments are not included in the {+154}Gd Adopted |g    
154GD5cG radiations.                                                            
154GD cG RI(P)$Value is an upper limit, since it includes a contribution from   
154GD2cG {+153}Gd.                                                              
154GD cG RI(Q)$|g is doubly placed with I|g undivided; second placement is not  
154GD2cG indicated by authors.                                                  
154GD cG RI(R)$From branching in {+154}Tb |e decay (21.5 h), I|g=12.2~{I16} is  
154GD2cG expected, so |g is probably a doublet.                                 
154GD cL E$Calculated from a least-squares fit to the listed E|g values. Four   
154GD2cL out of 452 E|g values differ from the calculated ones by more than 3|s.
154GD cL J$From the authors and based on |g multipolarities, previous           
154GD2cL assignments, and proposed band structure. If assignments differ from   
154GD3cL those in {+154}Gd Adopted Levels, this is noted (a difference involving
154GD4cL parentheses only is not noted).                                        
