154GD  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154GD c  {+154}Gd(e,e') measurements have been made with E(e)=78-380~MeV to     
154GD2c  study collective levels below 1~MeV (1986He09. Other: 1983He21) and    
154GD3c  with E(e)=25-48~MeV to study 1+ levels (1989Ha20).                     
154GD c  Theory and model calculations related to M1 excitations include:       
154GD2c  1987Ha38, 1987Ra30, 1988We08, 1989Bl01, 1989De42, 1989Ra01, 1990Fa09,  
154GD3c  1990Li07, 1990Vl01, 1991De05, and 1991Ra03.                            
154GD D  Experimental methods:                                                  
154GD D  1983He21: (e,e') with various energies and angles on enriched (99.4%)  
154GD2D       target. Report data on 2+ levels at 123, 816, and 996 keV.        
154GD D  1986He09: (e,e'), E(e)=78-380 MeV on enriched (99.35%) target.  e'     
154GD2D       measured with resolution as good as 6E-05.  Report cross section  
154GD3D       vs E(e) for 7 levels below 1 MeV and associated B(E2), B(E4), and 
154GD4D       B(E6) values.                                                     
154GD D  1989Ha20: (e,e'), E(e)=25-48 MeV to measure B(M1) for 1+ levels.       
154GD2D       Report 1 or 4 levels and B(M1) values.                            
154GD D  1991De05: Model calculations for 1+ states.                            
154GD cL $Levels below 1~MeV are members of the ground-state band, the          
154GD2cL |b-vibrational band (681 and 816~keV), and |g-vibrational band (996    
154GD3cL keV). B(M1) values are from 1989Ha20 and B(E2), B(E4), and B(E6) values
154GD4cL are from 1986He09.                                                     
154GD cL J$From the authors' assignments, except those in parentheses which are 
154GD2cL the evaluator's assignments based on comments of 1989Ha20.  Values     
154GD3cL agree with the adopted values, except as noted.                        
154GD cL E(R)$Estimated by evaluator from fig. 3 of 1989Ha20.                   
