154GD    154TB EC DECAY (9.973 H)      1975SO03,1972VY04,1973LA2025NDS    202503
154GD  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154GD D  DATA SET UPDATED (APRIL, 2008) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE A NEW Q VALUE,   
154GD2D   DATA ON A NEW 1701 LEVEL, WHICH ALSO INVOLVES A DIFFERENT PLACEMENT   
154GD3D   OF SOME GAMMAS, AND REVISED COMMENTS.                                 
154GD c  Three {+154}Tb isomers (21.5, 9.973, and 22.7 h) have been observed.   
154GD2c  The most complete decomposition of the |g data among these isomers     
154GD3c  is from 1975So03, so these data are used to place the |g.              
154GD c  A study of the {+154}Tb isomers is reported as a part of the thesis    
154GD2c  which constitutes 2001KuZS. With the exception of information relating 
154GD3c  to the 1701 level, these data are not included here, since further     
154GD4c  analysis appears to be required. The data regarding the 1701 level is  
154GD5c  taken from the study of 2003Ku19, together with information from a     
154GD6c  private communication from J.L. Wood, one of the authors of this study.
154GD D  Experimental methods:                                                  
154GD D  See 154TB EC DECAY (21.5 H) for tally of references.                   
154GD cE TI$Values are from |g-transition-intensity balances. Due to the        
154GD2cE incompleteness of the decay scheme, values less than 2% are considered 
154GD3cE unreliable and are not given. For the same reason, uncertainties are   
154GD4cE not given for values less than 5%.                                     
154GD cE TI$As a check of the normalization, it is noted that |S\ I(|e+|b{++})  
154GD2cE is 81% {I14} for the values given, 100% {I14} for all positive values  
154GD3cE computed, and 97% {I14} for all values computed including three small  
154GD4cE negative ones.                                                         
154GD cE TI$The total-absorption |g spectrum of 1980By03 indicates that for a   
154GD2cE {+154}Tb source of unstated isomer content, the feeding is primarily to
154GD3cE levels near 2.0~MeV. This measured feeding appears compatible with any 
154GD4cE combination of the three {+154}Tb isomers.                             
154GD cG $I|g values are not given for several |g's by 1975So03. These |g's are 
154GD2cG known from other studies to deexcite levels observed in this decay, but
154GD3cG for various reasons are not seen in this decay (1975So03).             
154GD cG E$From weighted average of values of 1972Vy04 and 1975So03.  Values    
154GD2cG without uncertainties were computed from level energies by 1975So03.   
154GD cG E$Because of the more definitive isomer assignment only the unplaced   
154GD2cG |g's of 1975So03 are given.                                            
154GD cG E(T)$From 2003Ku19. The uncertainties are nominal values (from a       
154GD2cG private communication from J.L. Wood, one of the authors of 2003Ku19). 
154GD cG RI(U)$Computed by the evaluator from the relative B(E2) values in      
154GD2cG 2003Ku19, normalized to I|g(983.7|g)=0.6.                              
154GD cG M,MR$Assignments and values are from {+154}Gd adopted |g radiations and
154GD2cG include the results of all types of experiments and all decay modes.   
154GD3cG See {+154}Gd adopted |g radiations for other information including: (1)
154GD4cG mixing ratios such as |d(M3/E2) and |d(M2/E1) where |d can be zero and 
154GD5cG is not included here; (2) comments on measurements for lines which are 
154GD6cG multiplets; and (3) identification of |a values that are based on      
154GD7cG experimental values rather than theory.                                
154GD cL E$From least-squares fit to |g energies.                               
154GD cL J$From {+154}Gd Adopted Levels.                                        
