154TB c  Experimental methods:                                                  
154TB c  1982Be46: {+148}Nd({+11}B,5n|g) on enriched (90%) target with          
154TB2c       E({+11}B)=50-68 MeV. With Ge detectors measured E|g, I|g,         
154TB3c       |g|g coincidences, projectile-|g delayed coincidences, |g(|q),    
154TB4c       and excitation functions.                                         
154TB c  1999Ha04: {+124}Sn({+36}S,p5n|g) with E({+36}S)=160 and175 MeV.        
154TB2c       Measured |g's with Gammasphere spectrometer using 67 or 93        
154TB3c       Compton-suppressed Ge detectors.                                  
154TB cG E         Values are from 1982Be46, unless otherwise noted. |g's       
154TB2cG      reported only by 1999Ha04 are noted.                              
154TB cG RI        Values are from 1982Be46. The authors state that the         
154TB2cG      uncertainties are "10% to 30% depending on the line strength      
154TB2cG      and the complexity of the spectrum." The evaluator have           
154TB3cG      interpreted this as 10% for I|g |> 30, 20% for 30 > I|g |> 10,    
154TB4cG      and 30% for I|g < 10.                                             
154TB cG M         Assigned E2 by evaluator based on A{-2}/A{-0} > 0.15         
154TB2cG      (1982Be46), which is interpreted as |DJ=2 transition.             
154TB cG E(Q)      From 1999Ha04 only.                                          
154TB cG E(R)      From 1982Be46 only.                                          
154TB cG E(W)$|g placed from the 0+x (9-) level by 1982Be46, but no other       
154TB2cG information is given regarding this |g or the level populated by IT.   
154TB cG E(A)$From 1999Ha04; other: 732 from 1982Be46, but questionable there.  
154TB cG RI(S)     Value may include contribution from {+155}Tb.                
154TB cL E         The absolute energies of the levels seen in these studies    
154TB2cL      have not been determined. Values, relative to 9- or 7+ levels,    
154TB3cL      are computed from |g energies.                                    
154TB cL J         The spin and parity of each bandhead are assumed             
154TB2cL      (1982Be46 and 1999Ha04), with the 9- band proposed to be          
154TB3cL      analogous to a 9- band in {+152}Eu and the 7+ band to be          
154TB4cL      analogous to one in {+156}Tb.                                     
154TB cL E(N)      From 1999Ha04 only.                                          
