154DY cL           Using the recoil-distance technique in combination with      
154DY2cL      large transient magnetic fields, 1993Bi09 measured g-factors of   
154DY3cL      excited states up to high spins. The measurement was sensitive    
154DY4cL      only to states populated |? 13.5 ps after the reaction. The       
154DY5cL      reported values were normalized to g=0.36 {I4} (a theoretical     
154DY6cL      value) for the 2+ member of the ground state band. Relative to    
154DY7cL      this value, the g-factors for the respective states (labeled by   
154DY8cL      the J|p value or range) are as follows: 0.39 {I6}, 4+; 0.35       
154DY9cL      {I9}, 6+ through 8+; 0.19 {I13}, 10+ through 14+; 0.11 {I14},     
154DY0cL      16+ through 20+; 0.28 {I13}, 22+ through 30+; 0.44 {I11}, 32+     
154DYAcL      through 36+; 0.23 {I10}, 9- through 15-; 0.32 {I13}, 17-          
154DYBcL      through 21-; and 0.16 {I8}, 27- through 35-. From the data of     
154DYCcL      1984Ha39 and the evaluation of 1989Ra16, the reported average     
154DYDcL      g-factor for levels with a mean J of 26 is 0.39 {I5}.             
