154DY  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154DY D  DATA SET UPDATED (NOVEMBER, 2007) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE BRICC ICC     
154DY2D   VALUES, REVISED CONFIGURATION ASSIGNMENTS, MANY REVISED COMMENTS,     
154DY3D   AND COMMENTS REGARDING THE 2183 LEVEL.                                
154DY c  Experimental methods:                                                  
154DY c  1968Wa12: Produced by {+148}Sm({+11}B,5n) and ({+10}B,4n) with         
154DY2c       E({+11}B)=75 MeV and E({+10}B)=60 MeV. |g singles and             
154DY3c       |g|g coincidences measured with Ge and NaI(Tl) detectors.         
154DY4c       Report 19 |g's.                                                   
154DY c  1974Sc19: Produced by {+147}Sm({+10}B,3n) with E({+10}B)=41 and 45     
154DY2c       MeV. |g measured with Ge detector; report 19 |g's.                
154DY c  1980Zo02: From the {+154}Er |e decay, with the source material         
154DY2c       produced in the {+148}Sm({+12}C,6n) reaction with E({+12}C)=83    
154DY2c       MeV. Measured |g singles and |g|g coincidences with Ge detectors  
154DY3c       and ce with Si(Li) detectors. Reported 32 |g's, 16 with           
154DY4c       multipolarities. Preliminary reports: 1975ZoZT and 1977ZoZY.      
154DY c  1981ZuZU: Abstract which reports E|g and I|g for 28 |g's and 511       
154DY2c       annihilation line; 3 |g's and 511 are not reported by 1980Zo02.   
154DY c  1983Al06, 1983AlZP: Measured |b{++} end-point with Ge detector.        
154DY c  1983GaZR: Measured ce with Si(Li) detector and reported |a{-K} and     
154DY2c       |a{-L} values.                                                    
154DY c  1991AlZY: Measured |b{++} end-points with Ge detector to determine     
154DY2c       isomer excitation energy.                                         
154DY cE E$From 1983Al06.                                                       
154DY cG           The indicated |g|g coincidence results are from a general    
154DY2cG      statement (1980Zo02), rather than explicit results.               
154DY cG E,RI      From evaluator's average of the data of 1980Zo02,            
154DY2cG   1974Sc19, and 1981ZuZU, but primarily from 1980Zo02.                 
154DY cG RI$I|g(511)=25.5 {I5} (1981ZuZU). However, from the calculated         
154DY2cG capture/positron ratios, we expect I(|b{++}) > 50 and thus             
154DY3cG I|g(511) > 100.                                                        
154DY cG M         Assignments are from Adopted Gammas. However, they are       
154DY2cG      primarily from |a{-K}(exp) from this decay mode (1980Zo02).       
154DY3cG      Other: 1983GaZR.                                                  
154DY cG CC(R)     Based on |a{-K}(exp) (1980Zo02).                             
154DY cG CC(S)     Based on |a{-K}(exp) (1980Zo02) from 3.10-m {+154}Ho |e      
154DY2cG  decay, where |g is not multiply placed.                               
154DY cL E         From least-squares fit to |g energies.                       
154DY cL J$From the adopted values. These are the same as proposed by 1980Zo02, 
154DY2cL which are based on |g multipolarities and expected band structure.     
154DY cL T$From the adopted values.                                             
154DY CL BAND(A)   Ground-state band.                                           
154DY CL BAND(B)$First excited 0+ band. Denoted as a quasi-|b band by 1980Zo02. 
154DY CL BAND(C)$Quasi-gamma band.                                              
154DY CL BAND(D)   Second excited 0+ band.                                      
154DY2cL  Several possibilities for configuration assignments for this band     
154DY3cL  are discussed by 1980Zo02.                                            
154DY CL BAND(E)   Octupole-based band, odd-spin band.                          
154DY CL BAND(F)   Octupole-related level sequence.                             
