154DY3c       |g|g coincidences measured with Ge and NaI(Tl) detectors.         
154DY4c       Report 19 |g's.                                                   
154DY c  1974Sc19: Produced by {+147}Sm({+10}B,3n) with E({+10}B)=41 and 45     
154DY2c       MeV. |g's measured with Ge detector; report 19 |g's.              
154DY c  1980Zo02: Produced by {+148}Sm({+11}B,5n) with E({+11}B)=83 MeV.       
154DY2c       Measured |g singles and |g|g coincidences with Ge detectors       
154DY3c       and ce with Si(Li) detectors. Reported 32 |g's, 16 with           
154DY4c       multipolarities. Preliminary reports: 1975ZoZT and 1977ZoZY.      
154DY c  1983Al06, 1983AlZP: Measured |b{++} end-point with Ge detector.        
154DY c  1983GaZR: Measured ce with Si(Li) detector and reported |a{-K} and     
154DY2c       |a{-L} values.                                                    
154DY c  1991AlZY: Measured |b{++} end-points with Ge detector to determine     
154DY2c       isomer excitation energy.                                         
154DY cE TI        Values are from computed |g-transition intensity balances.   
154DY2cE      However, values for levels with J|<6 are set to 0. As a result    
154DY3cE      of the method of normalizing the |g intensities and these         
154DY4cE      deletions, the sum of the |e+|b{++} intensities given is only     
154DY5cE      70%. Although other explanations are possible, most likely many   
154DY6cE      |g transitions have not been seen. This idea is supported by the  
154DY7cE      fact that many lower spin levels have positive computed feedings  
154DY8cE      which could be eliminated by |g feeding from higher-lying levels. 
154DY9cE      As a result of this ambiguity, no uncertainties are given.        
154DY cG E,RI      From evaluator's average of the data of 1968Wa12, 1974Sc19,  
154DY2cG      and 1980Zo02, but primarily from 1980Zo02.                        
154DY cG E         The 157.8 and 471.9 |g's reported by 1968Wa12 are assigned   
154DY2cG      to {+152}Tb (4.2 m) by 1980Zo02.                                  
154DY cG M         Assignments are from Adopted Gammas. However, they are       
154DY2cG      primarily from this decay mode from |a{-K}(exp) data              
154DY3cG      (1980Zo02).  Other: 1983GaZR.                                     
154DY cG CC(W)$Value computed assuming |d=1, with no uncertainty.               
154DY cG CC(R)     Based on |a{-K}(exp) (1980Zo02).                             
154DY cG CC(S)     Based on |a{-K}(exp) (1980Zo02) from 11.76-m decay,          
154DY2cG   where |g is not multiply placed.                                     
154DY cL E         From least-squares fit to |g energies.                       
154DY cL J$Values reported by 1980Zo02. Based on |g multipolarities and expected
154DY2cL band structure, including the results of nuclear-model calculations.   
154DY3cL These values are also the adopted ones, except for the 1334, 1743, and 
154DY4cL 2192 levels, which are shown here in parentheses.                      
154DY cL T$From the adopted values.                                             
154DY CL BAND(A)$Ground-state band.                                             
154DY CL BAND(B)$First excited 2+ band. Denoted as a quasi-|b band by 1980Zo02. 
154DY CL BAND(C)$Quasi-gamma band.                                              
154DY CL BAND(E)$Octupole-based band, odd-spin states.                          
154DY CL BAND(G)$Octupole-related level sequence.                               
154DY CL BAND(H)$7+ bandhead, probable configuration is (|n 3/2[532])+(|n       
154DY2cL 11/2[505]).                                                            
