154DY D  Data set updated by B. Singh (McMaster), Dec 31, 2009 to include SD    
154DY2D  band data from 2009Ij01                                                
154DY D  DATA SET RE-DONE (DECEMBER, 2007) BY CW REICH TO INCLUDE MOME2T,       
154DY2D   BETA2 VALUES FROM 1996Fi08 AND TO EXPAND THE COMMENTS AND CHANGE      
154DY3D   REMOVE MANY FLAG COMMENTS.                                            
154DY c  2009Ij01: {+122}Sn({+36}S,4n|g), E({+36}S)=165 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, 
154DY2c   |g|g using the Gammasphere spectrometer with 103 Compton-suppressed   
154DY2c   HPGe detectors. Authors report identification of six SD bands through 
154DY3c   considerations of |g|g coincidence relations, comparison of energy    
154DY4c   spacings and intensity patterns with other SD bands in the A |? 150   
154DY5c   region. Interpretation of bands with cranked relativistic mean-field  
154DY6c   theory using effective alignment method.                              
154DY d   Some of the authors in 2009Ij01 are the same as in 1995Ni03           
154DY c  1995Ni03: {+122}Sn({+36}S,4n|g), E({+36}S)=165 MeV. Measured |g's in   
154DY2c  the Gammasphere spectrometer with 36 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors.  
154DY3c  Authors report a sequence of 18 cascade |g's which, through            
154DY4c  considerations of coincidence relations, comparison of energy spacings 
154DY5c  and intensity patterns with other SD bands in the A |? 150 region, they
154DY6c  identify as an SD band.                                                
154DY c  1996Fi08: many of the same authors as 1995Ni03. As part of their study 
154DY2c  of {+155}Dy, using DSAM techniques, they also report population of the 
154DY3c  SD band in {+154}Dy previously identified by 1995Ni03. They deduce a   
154DY4c  value for the transition quadrupole moment (assumed to be constant)    
154DY5c  within this band and infer a value for the quadrupole deformation      
154DY6c  parameter from IT.                                                     
154DY c  All data are from 2009Ij01. In 1995Ni03 and 1996Fi08, only the         
154DY2c  SD-1 band was reported.                                                
154DY cG E$ From values received in e-mail reply from W.C. Ma on Oct 16, 2009.  
154DY2cG Values for SD-1 band were first reported in 1995Ni03, which are in     
154DY3cG agreement with those from 2009Ij01. Values from 1995Ni03 are listed    
154DY4cG under comments                                                         
154DY cG RI$ Values are relative to 100 for the population of normal-deformed   
154DY2cG g.s. band, and inferred by the evaluator from intensity profile        
154DY3cG figure 1 in 2009Ji01. For SD-1 band, values are also available from    
154DY4cG 1995Ni03 as an intensity plot. These values are listed under comments. 
154DY5cG The two sets of intensities are on a different scale, the values       
154DY6cG from 2009Ij01 are normalized to |?0.7 for the most intense |g rays     
154DY7cG in the cascade, whereas in 1995Ni03, these are normalized to |?1.      
154DY cL E$ From E|g's                                                          
154DY cL J$ As proposed by 2009Ij01 from assigned configurations and            
154DY2cL effective alignments                                                   
154DY cL $ Configurations are from 2009Ij01 based on assignments proposed in    
154DY2cL the theoretical interpretations by 1998Af02. These are labeled with    
154DY3cL respect to intruder configuration of |p6{+4}|n7{+2} for the yrast      
154DY4cL SD band in {+152}Dy, N=86                                              
