154DY    122SN(36S,4NG)                2002MA10,1987CR01,1985AZZY25NDS    202503
154DY  H TYP=FUL$AUT=N. NICA$CIT=NDS 200, 2 (2025)$CUT=22-Aug-2022$             
154DY D  DATA SET UPDATED (DECEMBER, 2007) BY CW REICH TO REWORK THE COMMENTS,  
154DY2D   ADD REFERENCE FLAGS AND RMS CHARGE-RADIUS VALUE.                      
154DY c  Data are from 2002Ma10 and 2002MaZM, unless otherwise noted.           
154DY c  This data set is based on the data set compiled from 2002Ma10 and      
154DY2c    from 2002MaZM, a datafile 154Dy_wm.ags on enriched (97%) target.     
154DY3c    http://radware.phy.ornl.gov, submitted by W. C. Ma, one of the       
154DY4c    authors of 2002Ma10 in March 2002 at the request of the compilers,   
154DY5c    R. Zywina and B. Singh (McMaster University) March, 2002.            
154DY c  2002Ma10: {+36}S({+122}Sn,4n|g), E({+122}Sn)=165 MeV. Measured E|g,    
154DY2c   I|g, |g|g, |g|g(|q)(DCO) using the Gammasphere array of 103           
154DY3c   Compton-suppressed Ge detectors.                                      
154DY c  2002MaZM: A datafile 154Dy_wm.ags on enriched (97%) target.            
154DY2c  http://radware.phy.ornl.gov, submitted by W. C. Ma one of the authors  
154DY3c  of 2002Ma10.                                                           
154DY c  1988Ma28: {+122}Sn({+36}S,4n|g) with E({+36}S)=165 MeV on enriched     
154DY2c       (>92%) target. Measured |g's in array of 8 Ge and 14 BGO          
154DY3c       detectors and deduced half-lives from Doppler-broadened line      
154DY4c       shapes.                                                           
154DY c  1987Cr01: {+110}Pd({+48}Ca,4n|g) with E({+48}Ca)=210 MeV on enriched   
154DY2c  (97%) target. Measured |g's including |g(|q) with an array of 6 Ge and 
154DY3c  50 BGO detectors.                                                      
154DY c  1985Az02: Lifetimes and feeding times measured by recoil-distance      
154DY2c        method following {+25}Mg({+134}Xe,5n|g) at 686 MeV with          
154DY3c        enriched (|>90%) target and {+124}Sn({+34}S,4n|g) at 146 MeV     
154DY4c        with enriched (99%) target. Lifetimes determined up to 18+       
154DY5c        and 17- levels. Values not given explicitly. Report by           
154DY6c        same authors: 1985KhZY.                                          
154DY c  1985AzZY: Thesis, see 1985Az02 for published form.                     
154DY d  1985Bo37:  Population of yrast states; no useful structure data.       
154DY2d       enriched (97%) target. Measured |g's including |g(|q) with        
154DY3d       array of 6 Ge and 50 BGO detectors.                               
154DY c  1983Kh03: Model discussion of scheme from 1982Pa10.                    
154DY c  1982Pa10: {+124}Sn({+34}S,4n|g) with E({+34}S)=145-165 MeV.            
154DY2c       Measured |g singles, |g|g(t), |g(|q) and excitation functions.    
154DY3c       Large NaI detector used as sum spectrometer and multiplicity      
154DY4c       filter. Report 45 |g's and about 34 levels.                       
154DY c  1978DuZY: Lifetimes measured by recoil-distance method with            
154DY2c       {+146}Nd({+12}C,4n|g). Preliminary values given for               
154DY3c       first 2+, 4+, and 6+ levels.                                      
154DY c  1974Ba07: {+154}Gd(|a,4n|g) with enriched (95%) target and             
154DY2c    E(|a)=46-56 MeV. Measured |g singles, |g(|q), and |g|g.              
154DY3c       Report 18 |g's and levels to 14+.                                 
154DY c  1974BeZF, 1975DaZM: {+156}Gd(|a,6n|g). Measured |g singles,            
154DY2D       |g(|q), |g(t), and |g|g coincidences. Report bands to 10+         
154DY2c       20+ and 15+.                                                      
154DY c  1973Kr12: {+146}Nd({+12}C,4n|g) with enriched target and               
154DY2c    E({+12}C)=57-109 MeV. Measured |g singles, |g(|q), and |g|g(t).      
154DY3c       Report 14 |g's and levels to 18+.                                 
154DY c  1968Wa12: {+139}La({+19}F,4n|g) with natural target and E({+19}F)      
154DY2c       |? 86 MeV. Measured excitation function and |g(|q). Report        
154DY3c       13 |g's and levels to 10+.                                        
154DY cG           For |g|g coincidence data, see 1973Kr12. Others: 1968Wa12,   
154DY2cG      1973Kr12.                                                         
154DY cG E,RI      From 2002MaZM. The data in 2002Ma10 have the energies only   
154DY2cG      to 1 keV, with no uncertainties and no intensities.               
154DY cG M         Deduced by evaluator from I|g(30|')/I|g(90|') data of        
154DY2cG      1987Cr01; assigned E2 (i.e., stretched Q interpreted as E2) if    
154DY3cG      ratio is |>0.70 and D (i.e., stretched D) if it is <0.70.         
154DY4cG      The level scheme of 1987Cr01 differs from that (2002Ma10)         
154DY5cG      given here; the evaluator has associated the multipolarities      
154DY6cG      with the same |g ray in its new location. Others: 1973Kr12        
154DY7cG      and 1974Ba07.                                                     
154DY cG M         The multipolarity assignments given in 2002MaZM are          
154DY2cG      suppressed in the present compilation because the RADWARE program 
154DY3cG      requires multipolarities for all |g's, even if there are          
154DY4cG      no supporting data.                                               
154DY cG E(X)      From {+154}Dy Adopted |g radiations                          
154DY cL E         From least-squares fit to E|g's; an uncertainty of 1 keV     
154DY2cL      is the default uncertainty when none is given. Seven E{-|g}       
154DY3cL   values out of 238 differ by 3|s or more from the calculated ones.    
154DY cL E         There are several levels reported in 1988Ma28 that are       
154DY2cL      not given in 2002Ma10. Since the first author is the same         
154DY3cL      for both papers, these levels are omitted here. The lowest        
154DY4cL      of these levels are at 2493, 2900, and 5589 keV.                  
154DY cL E(Q)$Maximally-aligned state; proposed termination of this level       
154DY2cL sequence.                                                              
154DY cL T         From 1985AzZY, unless noted as being from 1988Ma28.          
154DY2cL      See also 1985Az02 and 1982Pa10, where the T{-1/2} values are      
154DY3cL      reported in terms of transition-quadrupole moments.               
154DY cL           See 2002Ma10 for detailed multi-quasiparticle                
154DY2cL      configurations for different rotational bands, based on cranked   
154DY3cL      Nilsson-Strutinsky calculations.                                  
154DY cL T(R)      From 1988Ma28, Doppler-broadened line-shape analysis.        
154DY CL BAND(J)   First excited 0+ band.                                       
