154HO c  1994Ch50: E({+16}O)=67, 70, 73, 75 and 77 MeV on natural Pr target.    
154HO3c  Measured |g's with Tsukuba "ball" of six Compton-suppressed Ge         
154HO3c  detectors and determined excitation functions and DCO ratios, defined  
154HO4c  as I|g(0|')/I|g(117|'). Only the E|g and |g placements are reported.   
154HO c  2013Mo35: E({+16}O)=75 MeV beam from 12UD pelletron accelerator at     
154HO2c  University of Tsukuba, self supporting natural Pr target 2.7-          
154HO3c  mg/cm{+2} thick. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO)           
154HO4c  using the 11 HPGe detector array with BGO anti-Compton shields and     
154HO5c  low energy photon spectrometer (LEPS).                                 
154HO c  2013Mo35 and 1994Ch50 are related (same lab                            
154HO2c  and common authors) which are in very good agreement. Data and level   
154HO2c  scheme are from 2013Mo35                                               
154HO cG $DCO ratios for 37|' (or 143|') and 79|' (or 101|') geometry with gates
154HO2cG set only on stretched quadrupole transitions. Expected DCO ratios:     
154HO4cG |?1 for |DJ=2, stretched quadrupole transitions; |? 0.6 for |DJ=1,     
154HO5cG stretched dipole transition, and |?0.5-2.5 for |DJ=1, mixed            
154HO6cG dipole-quadrupole transition, depending on value of mixing ratio |d:   
154HO6cG 0.5 for |d=-1.0 and 2.5 for |d=1.0 (with no explicit |d values         
154HO6cG extracted)                                                             
