154YB cL           |a-particle emission from excited levels between 3 and       
154YB2cL      6 MeV in {+154}Yb populated in the {+154}Lu |e decay has been     
154YB3cL      reported by 1988Vi02. In addition, these authors report proton    
154YB4cL      emission from {+154}Yb states between 6.5 and 9 MeV excitation    
154YB5cL      energy. They measure I{-|a}=0.03% and I{-p}=0.06%. These          
154YB5cL      values were determined from the measured |a and proton            
154YB6cL      intensities, respectively, relative to I|g(821.3)(1+|a), which    
154YB7cL      they assume represents 100% of the {+154}Lu decays.               
