154YB2c       beam (300-ns pulses). |g's were detected using the OSIRIS         
154YB3c       |g-detector array. A large-volume four-sector neutron detector,   
154YB4c       located at 0|', was used to identify unknown evaporation          
154YB5c       channels. Only E|g values and a proposed level scheme are shown.  
154YB c  1996Zh09 report the results of a study of multiparticle yrast states   
154YB2c       involving the |p h{-11/2}, |n h{-9/2} and |n f{-7/2} shell-model  
154YB3c       orbitals in the four N=84 nuclides from {+151}Ho through          
154YB4c       {+154}Yb. The level scheme was established via coincidence,       
154YB5c       |g(|q), and intensity information on the |g's measured using      
154YB6c       the 20-detector Nordball array. A diagram identifies              
154YB7c       yrast levels up through the J=(24+) level.                        
154YB c  1993Zh10 and (especially) 1996Zh09 give an extensive discussion of     
154YB2c       the results of the shell-model calculations as they apply to      
154YB3c       the level scheme of {+154}Yb and the other N=84 nuclides from     
154YB4c       {+151}Ho to {+154}Tm.                                             
