154LU cL J$From a consideration of measured and calculated proton emission      
154LU2cL half-lives for the 10.5~ms state of {+166}Ir, 1997Da07 conclude that   
154LU3cL the proton emission is from the |p d{-3/2}, rather that from a |p      
154LU4cL s{-1/2} or |p h{-11/2} orbital. This, together with systematics which  
154LU5cL indicates that the odd neutron is in the |n f{-7/2} orbital, suggests  
154LU6cL that this {+166}Ir state has Configuration=((|p d{-3/2})(|n f{-7/2})). 
154LU7cL For this configuration, the Nordheim strong rule for angular-momentum  
154LU8cL coupling in odd-odd nuclides indicates that the J{+|p}=2- coupling lies
154LU9cL lower in energy. Hence, the {+166}Ir ground state most likely has      
154LUacL J{+|p}=2-. Since this level is fed by a succession of three unhindered 
154LUbcL (|DL=0) |a decays from the {+166}Ir ground state, its J{+|p} should be 
154LUccL the same.                                                              
