154LU cL J$1988Vi02 report significant |e+|b{++} feeding from {+154}Lu to the   
154LU2cL (6+) and (8+) levels in {+154}Yb and from this conclude that J{+|p} for
154LU3cL the {+154}Lu parent is (7+). They also indicate that this |e+|b{++}    
154LU4cL feeding pattern suggests a similar structure for these two final       
154LU5cL states. The odd proton and odd neutron in the {+154}Lu parent state are
154LU6cL in the |p h{-11/2} and |n f{-7/2} orbitals, respectively. The implied  
154LU7cL low log| {Ift} values indicate strong Gamow-Teller transitions, which  
154LU8cL in this case would be |p h{-11/2}|)|n h{-9/2}. It is now believed,     
154LU9cL however, that the configurations of the two {+154}Yb final states are  
154LU2cL quite different (see the discussion in the {+106}Cd({+54}Fe,|a2p|g)    
154LU2cL data set, as well as those in the original studies                     
154LU2cL (1993Zh10,1996Zh09)). Only one of these states, the (8+) level, can be 
154LU2cL fed by a strong Gamow-Teller transition. The transition to the (6+)    
154LU2cL level would be |p h{-11/2}|)|n f{-7/2}. It will be much weaker (and,   
154LU2cL possibly, may not take place). Thus, the basis for a (7+) assignment   
154LU2cL appears to be considerably weakened. The evaluator has chosen to       
154LU2cL adopt J{+|p}=(9+) for the {+154}Lu |e decay parent, in agreement with  
154LU2cL the systematics of the spins in this mass region.                      
