154LU cL $There may be some question as to whether the lowest level reported    
154LU2cL here (the (9+) level) is the same as the level that decays via |e to   
154LU3cL {+154}Yb. In their study of the {+154}Lu |e decay, 1988Vi02 assign the 
154LU4cL |e parent level as (7+). With this in mind, 1990Mc02 state that their  
154LU5cL results shed no light on this question, since a low-energy, highly     
154LU6cL converted transition (from (9+) to (7+)) would not have been detected  
154LU7cL in their work. However, the evaluator has concluded, based on the      
154LU8cL information from the in-beam studies (1993Zh10,1996Zh09) of the        
154LU9cL {+154}Yb level scheme, that the J{+|p} value of the {+154}Lu parent in 
154LUacL the |e decay is probably not (7+) but rather is (9+). Throughout this  
154LUbcL evaluation, it has been assumed that the (9+) level seen here is the   
154LUccL same as the parent state of the {+154}Lu |e decay.                     
