154HF c  Produced in the {+102}Pd({+54}Fe,2n) reaction with 240-245~MeV {+54}Fe 
154HF2c  ions on a 1-mg/cm{+2} {+102}Pd target. The reaction products were      
154HF3c  separated using the Daresbury Recoil Mass Separator. The source        
154HF4c  material was collected on an Al catcher foil. |g radiation was studied 
154HF5c  using a LEPS and four large Ge detectors. The time relationships       
154HF6c  between the signals from a position-sensitive detector and the |g-ray  
154HF7c  detectors were used for mass, T{-1/2} and |g|g coincidence             
154HF8c  determinations.                                                        
154HF cG E$The existence and energies of the |g-rays were established on the    
154HF2cG basis of peaks having only a few (typically 4-6) counts in the spectra.
154HF3cG These presumably represent only the dominant decay path of the isomer. 
154HF cL E$The ordering of the |g's, and thus the level energies, is based on   
154HF2cL the systematics of the lighter doubly even nuclides, especially        
154HF3cL {+150}Er and {+152}Yb.                                                 
154HF cL J$Adopted values, based on the systematics of the level schemes of the 
